{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent","id":1075671,"title":"Another GMC Tangent","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-09T19:04:30-07:00","id":1075671,"title":"Another GMC Tangent","content":"Bit of a tangent here, but the urge to post this has been bugging me for several days now. So I thought I'd get it over with and post my thoughts on the God Machine Chronicle.<br /> <br /> So I told myself I wouldn't be purchasing the<b> God Machine Chronicle</b> for reasons I will get to in a moment, but I've recently had little choice in the matter. With the Chronicles of Darkness moving its game lines onto second edition, I went ahead and bought the new rule book, along with Beast: the Primordial. My initial thoughts on the God Machine was that it was essentially the <b>World of Darkness: Matrix</b> edition, because everything I've heard come out of the game sounded like cyber-techno jargan. Infrastructure, embeds, codes, programs, glitches, radio signals. Everything sounded like the world was one big virtual simulation, but the people on Onyx Path insisted that this was not the case and that telling people it was the Matrix was unfair to the creators of the GMC<br /> <br /> So I decided to give the chronicle a read and I can say that I'm still not interested in it. From what I discovered after reading through the God Machine, it seems to be set in the realm of science fiction. Hell, there is even a quote near the start of the chapter that talks about how sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic!<br /> <br /> When I bought WoD, I did so because it was a supernatural world set in the modern era. The God Machine Chronicle takes that world and tries to turn it into a <b>Shin Megami</b> spin off. If you think I'm exaggerating, there is actually an example scenario in the book that puts the fate of the world in humanity's hands. <i>The choices are eternal chaos, order, or free will</i>; the same possible choices you get to make at the end of Shin Megami when you choose to side with Demons, Angels, or Humanity! When I searched around online for the opinions of others who have played the game, one person told me that the GMC is basically an attempt to include a monotheistic deity into the game without offending any real world groups. And I've got to say I agree with that assessment.<br /> <br /> It is precisely because of its connection to GMC that I have no interest in ever buying <b>Demon: the Descent.</b> Which is disappointing, because I would normally find the idea of playing a demon to be pretty friggin metal. I just don't want to play a demon who's <i>actually made out of metal.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> I've come up with a simple solution for the problem, though. I simply ignore any and all references to the God Machine in my Chronicles of Darkness setting. If I want to incorporate a God, Demon or Angel into the story, I use <i>Spirits</i>, <i>Fey</i>, or similar creatures to substitute for them. It would not be hard to convince people that the seemingly omnipotent True Fey are deities, just as it would not be hard to use Ephemeral Beings to convince people of being demonic or angelic figures. So, to reiterate, the God Machine does not exist for me, nor do Angels and Demons as they are presented in that setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry if that sounded like whining, or if it's already been said a hundred times; but I at least gave it a read. I will say, however, that before doing so, I hated the GMC because of my misconceptions about its premise. Now that I know more about it, my feelings have moved from hatred, to simply disinterest. I enjoy Shin Megami, I just don't feel like it needed a cross over with World of Darkness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T20:18:11-07:00","id":1075694,"title":"","content":"You're not obligated to like everything. I still think your takeaway is a rather superficial reading, but hey, I don't like everything either. I didn't like the This Is Hell hook either, for what it's worth, though my objection was that it was written in much too broad strokes with little practical attention to helping the ST with what would actually occur in play.<br /> <br /> Not sure what discussion you expect will come out of starting a separate thread for this. Not really anything there to say except &quot;nuh-uh&quot; and &quot;yuh-huh.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T20:37:53-07:00","id":1075699,"title":"","content":"I could see why you would think that way about Demon the Descent, but the God Machine Chronicle is just an easy-to-use reason for weirdness, and while 'Infrastructure, embeds, codes, programs, glitches, radio signals,' can be technical terms, within the game they are not part of science fiction any more than leylines, blood magic, sorcery, demons, and radio signals are. Most of them are tied into Demon, anyways.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine as a concept can be excised without any issue in most games. The exceptions being games like Demon or other games you decide to incorporate the God-Machine in.<br /> <br /> I don't understand how you could come away thinking otherwise.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, the conflict between order, chaos, and 'free will' has been a common thread in fiction and games for decades before Shin Megami Tensei was a thing. It's the basis of the Dungeons and Dragons alignment chart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-09-2017, 11:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T20:59:23-07:00","id":1075705,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think your reading is shallow and uncharitable, but at the end of the day, who cares. You don't have to like the God-Machine to play Second Edition, as it has little to no connection with any gameline other than Demon. Plenty of people have gamelines in Chronicles that they dislike and ignore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T21:08:40-07:00","id":1075711,"title":"","content":"You say you want 'real' demons and angels.<br /> <br /> No, what you really want is demons and angels of Abrahamic faiths, dressed in modern Western aesthetics that evolved from Medieval European aesthetics.<br /> <br /> GMC and DtD gives you demons and angels of Gnosticism, dressed in post-modern technological aesthetics that share some traits but not themes with Science Fiction. <i>Of course </i>you end up being disinterested in them.<br /> <br /> And I see that you've mistaked the medium for the message - DtD and GMC have a lot of technology and techno-magic going on, but the ultimate theme is Gnosticism (ie. the interplay between knowledge and spirituality)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And even with analogies to the SMT series, I think you've missed some points. The SMT series apply technology to the occult. GMC and DtD assume the two are one and the same. It's the difference from simplifying summoning rituals into a computer program, and writing a new summoning ritual with computer language.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T21:11:59-07:00","id":1075714,"title":"","content":"I've done this fight enough times that not only do I not care to retread it, but I actually imagine you probably know my immediate counter-arguments.<br /> <br /> I <i>did</i> like This Is Hell, though, and likewise I'm pretty sure that conflict is almost older than dirt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T22:48:38-07:00","id":1075738,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this reading of it is pretty surface-level. I mean, there's a lot of &quot;sci-fi&quot; sounding elements, but for the most part, the tech-y element of the God-Machine could be stripped away without changing the core parts of it. The Demons would still be Demons. The Angels would still be Angels. The Infrastructure would be largely the same in all but name and aesthetic trappings.<br /> <br /> Really, it seems like the main issue I'm seeing for Nyrufa is one of the least significant elements of the GMC not appealing to them.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, Demon is a little more wrapped up in the &quot;Tech&quot; part of &quot;Techgnostic Espionage&quot;, but even then, it doesn't strictly require the Demons and the God-Machine to be technological in appearance to work. The Demons would be able to function in almost the exact same way without it. Gnosticism dates back centuries, stories about world-spanning conspiracies date back even further, and espionage has existed for as long as there have been people wanting to know what others are up to.<br /> <br /> So I don't particularly see the issue. People generally have little problem refluffing a bit of setting they dislike, or even heavily rejiggering core pieces of a game's themes or assumptions, like the contingent of people who want more transhumanist stuff in Promethean*, so this particular issue seems relatively small and easily worked around.<br /> <br /> If you don't like GMC or Demon, that's fine, but it bugs me to see all these designers putting in all the work they did, and seeing it get dismissed with such a shallow appraisal.<br /> <br /> * <sup>I'm not saying they're wrong or right for wanting it, just that they exist, and that they want something that changes the core assumptions of Promethean, and so it serves as an example of what I'm talking about</sup>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T23:27:49-07:00","id":1075749,"title":"","content":"I can't say I liked &quot;This is Hell&quot; too much either. I've never heard of Shin Megami, but the whole plot of choosing between Heaven and Hell, with the secret revelation being that Humanity was a third option the whole time, is a story I've seen played out plenty of times in a variety of media.<br /> <br /> That said, I <i>did</i> like the God-Machine as an idea. As others have said it's principally a way to facilitate High Weirdness, not Science Fiction. A lot of its plots and machinations appear 100% occult from the outside. The point of that Arthur C. Clarke quote was to show that sacrificing virgins at clocktowers to appease a nameless deity is magic to us, even if the entity being &quot;appeased&quot; is actually using those sacrifices in a formulaic, even scientific, manner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-09T23:50:30-07:00","id":1075757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075711#post1075711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say you want 'real' demons and angels.<br /> <br /> No, what you really want is demons and angels of Abrahamic faiths, dressed in modern Western aesthetics that evolved from Medieval European aesthetics.<br /> <br /> GMC and DtD gives you demons and angels of Gnosticism, dressed in post-modern technological aesthetics that share some traits but not themes with Science Fiction. <i>Of course </i>you end up being disinterested in them.<br /> <br /> And I see that you've mistaked the medium for the message - DtD and GMC have a lot of technology and techno-magic going on, but the ultimate theme is Gnosticism (ie. the interplay between knowledge and spirituality)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And even with analogies to the SMT series, I think you've missed some points. The SMT series apply technology to the occult. GMC and DtD assume the two are one and the same. It's the difference from simplifying summoning rituals into a computer program, and writing a new summoning ritual with computer language.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> No, I'm not specifying western demons in particular. There's all different kinds of cultural demons that I would be happy implementing. I don't know where you thought I was singling out the Abrahamic ones. The ones I'm refusing to accept are the 'ghost in the machine', rogue AI type of demons, which is the idea that keeps springing to mind the more I read about the God Machine and its servants.<br /> <br /> <br /> And as for blending technology and the occult together, that's another feature I don't care for very much. I don't like the idea of magic just being some super advanced technology we haven't figured out yet, which is exactly what the book alludes to the God Machine being at the start of the chapter. I'm willing to acknowledge that technology can <i>imitate magic</i>, but I do not acknowledge them as being one in the same. When I think of magic, I think of beings with the power to warp the fabric of reality itself to their imagination, such as the True Fey, or those of the Supernal Realms. Making it a form of technology, or applying a scientific explanation to it instantly makes it less special to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> And as for the comparison to SMT, there is more than just the This is Hell scenario. The SMT franchise seems to heavily portray Demons, Angels, and even the gods themselves as some kind of super advanced technology. You summon demons with a smart phone, they appear as data clouds, the Angels look like androids, you can break them down into programming code and fuse them together in cyber space, and I think at one point they even mention something about an Axiom, which I am lead to believe is some kind of super computer that keeps reality running!<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> I wasn't trying to stir up any heated arguments or angrily bashing the GMC. I simply felt an urge to write my thoughts on the matter and post them. I didn't think posting this in any of the splat threads would have made much sense, so I posted them in this section, instead.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-10-2017, 03:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T00:03:16-07:00","id":1075758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075757#post1075757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> When I think of magic, I think of beings with the power to warp the fabric of reality itself to their imagination, such as the True Fey, or those of the Supernal Realms. Making it a form of technology, or applying a scientific explanation to it instantly makes it less special to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;technology&quot; and &quot;scientific explanation&quot; you're talking about is, literally and without exaggeration, &quot;(a) God did it.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T00:12:26-07:00","id":1075760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075758#post1075758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;technology&quot; and &quot;scientific explanation&quot; you're talking about is, literally and without exaggeration, &quot;(a) God did it.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> A God who manipulates causality to nudge events to playing out the way it wants them to. The book even says the God Machine is, in fact, NOT all knowing, all powerful, all present. It has limitations and it needs agents to overcome those limitations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T00:34:36-07:00","id":1075765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075760#post1075760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A God who manipulates causality to nudge events to playing out the way it wants them to.</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is different from what any non-machine deity does... how, exactly?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075760#post1075760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The book even says the God Machine is, in fact, NOT all knowing, all powerful, all present. It has limitations and it needs agents to overcome those limitations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plenty of magical beings in fiction and real-world religion are not all knowing, all powerful, or all present and need agents to overcome their limitations. Far, far more than there are omnipotent, omniscient, omnipresent entities. Is Odin not special either because there are limitations to his power?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T00:37:31-07:00","id":1075767,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075757#post1075757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I'm not specifying western demons in particular. There's all different kinds of cultural demons that I would be happy implementing. I don't know where you thought I was singling out the Abrahamic ones. The ones I'm refusing to accept are the 'ghost in the machine', rogue AI type of demons, which is the idea that keeps springing to mind the more I read about the God Machine and its servants.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I admit that I overreacted on Abrahamic angels and stuff. Been a sore spot.<br /> <br /> Still, let's look at the rogue AI demons you mention. If the fallen angels are AI, then angels must be AI creatures, right? So you would also deny AI angels, correct? But then, what is an AI? Artificial intelligence, of course. A consciousness that has been created whole cloth, not born and grown like our own forms of consciousness. We humans automatically equate &quot;artificial&quot; with machinery and electronics, but let's think outside human limits. If God spontaneously creates an angel, using numinous energies and mystic alignments, isn't that angel an artificial intelligence? Just not man-made, but God-made?<br /> <br /> It's not that DtD's flavor of angels (and demons) are modeled after AI. Rather, I dare say it's the other way around; what we humans call AI are man-made angels.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And as for blending technology and the occult together, that's another feature I don't care for very much. I don't like the idea of magic just being some super advanced technology we haven't figured out yet, which is exactly what the book alludes to the God Machine being at the start of the chapter. I'm willing to acknowledge that technology can <i>imitate magic</i>, but I do not acknowledge them as being one in the same. When I think of magic, I think of beings with the power to warp the fabric of reality itself to their imagination, such as the True Fey, or those of the Supernal Realms. Making it a form of technology, or applying a scientific explanation to it instantly makes it less special to me. </div> </div> </div>A quick look at Wikipedia says that technology is &quot;the collection of techniques, skills, methods and processes used in the production of goods or services or in the accomplishment of objectives&quot;. Let's say a witch-doctor peruses through his grimoire where all his potion recipes, language of the spirits, how to reach ecstasy by dancing, and designs for sacred drawings to create wards against illness are written down, and uses it to produce an amulet of plague-warding and heal the sick by laying on hands, he is by definition using a form of technology. But this doesn't prevent it from being occult, does it?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And as for the comparison to SMT, there is more than just the This is Hell scenario. The SMT franchise seems to heavily portray Demons, Angels, and even the gods themselves as some kind of super advanced technology. You summon demons with a smart phone, they appear as data clouds, the Angels look like androids, you can break them down into programming code and fuse them together in cyber space, and I think at one point they even mention something about an Axiom, which I am lead to believe is some kind of super computer that keeps reality running! </div> </div> </div>Yeah... nope. All the demons, angels, and gods you summon are exactly that. The Demon Summoning Program, a key element in the franchise, is nothing but a modernized version of ancient summoning rituals. While humans use high-tech equipment to interact with demons, that's just a way to translate the supernatural into something humans can grasp. The data clouds that demons appear as that you mention? Of course they appear like glitched screens and statics, because <i>that's how the super-tech visor that humans use perceive unknown variables in the first place</i>. Not because they really are living clouds of data. Angels looking like robots? Okay, now you're onto something, but see what I said about angels and AI. Fusion involving breaking demons down into programming code? Nah, it's more like breaking their ectoplasmic bodies down and melting their souls in a pot. The programming code is where, like the Summoning Program, makes the whole process a whole lot easier to reproduce reliably. No idea what you mean about an Axiom, so can't speak on that.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, DtD and GMC don't assume the computer codes are a shortcut for replicating occult rituals. No, the computer codes are themselves a primitive form of what God is using to create angels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":".  typo 04-10-2017, 03:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T00:40:05-07:00","id":1075769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075760#post1075760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A God who manipulates causality to nudge events to playing out the way it wants them to.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is, in fact, all of them worth talking about in this system.<br /> <br /> Even the Exarchs aren't exempt from the there's-a-story-here clause that prevents wholesale reality-alteration from being indistinguishable from the players suddenly playing a slightly-to-drastically-different game without comment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The book even says the God Machine is, in fact, NOT all knowing, all powerful, all present. It has limitations and it needs agents to overcome those limitations. </div> </div> </div>Yup.<br /> <br /> None of those limitations cannot be summarized with the same confines that the other Megahuge Supernatural Gribblies deal with.<br /> <br /> None of those limitations mean the criteria for what does and does not create working Infrastructure are not for all intents and purposes completely arbitrary.<br /> <br /> None of those limitations change the fact that the Machine is nigh-infinitely complex and compartmentalized in such a manner that makes gadgets functionally identical to gifts from the gods rather than mundanely-reproducible processes that can be universally applied without getting sponsored by God (which would defeat the point of the exercise).<br /> <br /> The God-Machine is distinguished by its proximity to the material world and its degree of entwinement with mortal society and the occult/physical laws of the universe. It produces demons when it runs up against the imperfections of the world that give rise to fire and screaming and pain, and those demons are equipped to claim souls and speak in tongues and dramatically alter human lives. The fact that God speaks in solar winds and radio waves and traffic noise doesn't actually detract from the grandeur of its being able to move mountains and facilitate the slaying of dragons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T00:40:42-07:00","id":1075770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075760#post1075760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A God who manipulates causality to nudge events to playing out the way it wants them to. The book even says the God Machine is, in fact, NOT all knowing, all powerful, all present. It has limitations and it needs agents to overcome those limitations.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see, so you mean that a &quot;real&quot; Divinity has to be omniscient, omnipotent, and omnipresent. Who can just wish things into existence, without having to leverage pieces of the world like a chessboard.<br /> <br /> You have just claimed that the vast majority of deities ever worshipped by humanity are not truly divine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T00:42:27-07:00","id":1075771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075765#post1075765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is different from what any non-machine deity does... how, exactly?<br /> <br /> <br /> Plenty of magical beings in fiction and real-world religion are not all knowing, all powerful, or all present and need agents to overcome their limitations. Far, far more than there are omnipotent, omniscient, omnipresent entities. Is Odin not special either because there are limitations to his power?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1 - Because I was lead to believe that the monotheistic, non-machine deities can literally make their wills manifest. They don't need to carefully stack the dominos in place. If they want something to happen, it happens<br /> <br /> <br /> 2 - Yeah, I'm aware of that, but most of those who aren't omnipotent / omnipresent / omniscient are part of a collective pantheon, rather than being considered a singular individual. In my personal experience, monotheistic cultures tend to portray whatever deity they follow as being in control of everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T00:52:03-07:00","id":1075774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075771#post1075771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1 - Because I was lead to believe that the monotheistic, non-machine deities can literally make their wills manifest. They don't need to carefully stack the dominos in place. If they want something to happen, it happens<br /> <br /> <br /> 2 - Yeah, I'm aware of that, but most of those who aren't omnipotent / omnipresent / omniscient are part of a collective pantheon, rather than being considered a singular individual. In my personal experience, monotheistic cultures tend to portray whatever deity they follow as being in control of everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so you are confined to monotheistic interpretations of divinity. Too bad this isn't Demon The Fallen or In Nomine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T00:56:34-07:00","id":1075778,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075774#post1075774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so you are confined to monotheistic interpretations of divinity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Monotheistic interpretations of divinity that assume that regular causality is not already the means by which the Divine Will is propagated, no less.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T01:01:35-07:00","id":1075782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075757#post1075757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ones I'm refusing to accept are the 'ghost in the machine', rogue AI type of demons, which is the idea that keeps springing to mind the more I read about the God Machine and its servants.</div> </div> </div> </div>The technological stuff is almost entirely superficial. As far as how the demons of Descent actually function, they are very much Gnostic fallen angels. You don't have to like the aesthetic trappings of Descent's demons, it's even ok for those trappings to kill your interest in the game, but don't mistake the aesthetics for the themes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075757#post1075757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as for blending technology and the occult together, that's another feature I don't care for very much. I don't like the idea of magic just being some super advanced technology we haven't figured out yet, which is exactly what the book alludes to the God Machine being at the start of the chapter. I'm willing to acknowledge that technology can <i>imitate magic</i>, but I do not acknowledge them as being one in the same. When I think of magic, I think of beings with the power to warp the fabric of reality itself to their imagination, such as the True Fey, or those of the Supernal Realms. Making it a form of technology, or applying a scientific explanation to it instantly makes it less special to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, Clarke's Third Law isn't just a fictional concept used to blend magic and technology. It's a factual observation about the way science works. Science is an ongoing process of explaining observable phenomena. If beings existed with the power to warp the fabric of reality itself to their imagination, that would be a phenomenon, and if scientists observed it, they would seek to understand how it functions. If it could not be explained by current science, <i>science would change</i> to account for its possibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075757#post1075757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wasn't trying to stir up any heated arguments or angrily bashing the GMC. I simply felt an urge to write my thoughts on the matter and post them. I didn't think posting this in any of the splat threads would have made much sense, so I posted them in this section, instead.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a very old argument that has plagued the fandom since the release of GMC. If you don't want to stir up old arguments, maybe don't make posts bringing up historically heated subjects. If you don't want to angrily bash GMC maybe don't start threads that have no point but to say &quot;here's why I don't like GMC.&quot; If you don't like it that's fine, but you don't need to publicly announce exactly why you don't like it to a bunch of people who do like it and are sick of defending it against exactly the same criticism for the past four years.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T01:07:43-07:00","id":1075784,"title":"","content":"Upon reading Satchel's reply post to mine, I recall this old story:<br /> <br /> A man was trapped on his house's rooftops, with a flood ravaging the entire neighborhood. People call at him from below, telling him to come down since the water's not lethal yet and let's make a run for it. He stays, saying that God will send him aid. As the flood eventually rises up to consume houses just below their roofs, some people on a makeshift raft come over to him, saying that there's room for survivors. He stays, saying that God will send him aid. The waters have nearly finished drowning all houses, and a rescue team approaches in a helicopter with a ladder, telling him to get on. He stays, saying that God will send him aid. The man dies, goes to Heaven, and meets God. He asks why God did not send him aid in his most dire need. God is absolutely perplexed, and says that He did send aid. Three times, even.<br /> <br /> But this God is also not Godly enough for you, Nyrufa, if your idea of divinity is defined as manifesting miracles with nothing but will, without using the world itself as His instrument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T01:12:11-07:00","id":1075785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075771#post1075771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 - Because I was lead to believe that the monotheistic, non-machine deities can literally make their wills manifest. They don't need to carefully stack the dominos in place. If they want something to happen, it happens</div> </div> </div> </div>So you've never heard of Intelligent Design? How about the saying, &quot;God works in mysterious ways&quot;? Even if we're talking about the God of Christianity, the one perhaps most commonly attributed omnipotence, it takes a very, <i>very</i> broad interpretation to reach the conclusion that his power works by whim rather than by setting chains of events into motion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075757#post1075757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2 - Yeah, I'm aware of that, but most of those who aren't omnipotent / omnipresent / omniscient are part of a collective pantheon, rather than being considered a singular individual. In my personal experience, monotheistic cultures tend to portray whatever deity they follow as being in control of everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so. Most mono-theistic Gods, the Christian God included have limitations and frequently acts through angels or other proxies to circumvent those limitations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T01:27:42-07:00","id":1075790,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075757#post1075757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm willing to acknowledge that technology can <i>imitate magic</i>, but I do not acknowledge them as being one in the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Free Council would like to explain to you how wrong you are?<br /> <br /> I mean, given how much Mage deals with &quot;what is magic?&quot; in the CofD, there's an entire faction devoted to the idea that human art and technology is a form of magic because it's using Supernal laws (if filtered through the Fallen World first) to create things that can even influence the Supernal in turn as the Supernal has new elements added to it to encompass newly created achievements. <br /> <br /> I'm not trying to say anything about your personal preferences, but I am trying to point to a whole faction of mages that consider finding the magic in art, technology, and other expressions of human creativity to be a strong counter point to the idea that technology makes magic &quot;less special.&quot; If that narrative doesn't work for you, it doesn't. But maybe pointing this out might give you a different way to look at how the technological trappings of this stuff that might help you find a way to like it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And as for the comparison to SMT, there is more than just the This is Hell scenario. The SMT franchise seems to heavily portray Demons, Angels, and even the gods themselves as some kind of super advanced technology. You summon demons with a smart phone, they appear as data clouds, the Angels look like androids, you can break them down into programming code and fuse them together in cyber space, and I think at one point they even mention something about an Axiom, which I am lead to believe is some kind of super computer that keeps reality running! </div> </div> </div>While all of this could be done with the CofD rules, none of this is the default. Yeah, there's certainly some overlap with SMT on a surface level (I think you're going to keep getting this response)... but why exactly is that so bad? Demons are &quot;rogue AIs&quot; in a sense, but they're not computer programs. You can't control them with your smart phone (though they might let you think you can while they're using you through your smart phone...). Angels can appear as androids... or pretty much anything else normal, supernatural, or down right mind-bendingly impossible. The GMC offers a very different setup and moral conundrum than SMT does. The GM isn't good or evil. It isn't overtly malevolent, making Demons the good guys just because they're in opposition to it.<br /> <br /> The GM also doesn't just &quot;nudge.&quot; There's a city with multiple alternate timelines running parallel with each other and it's possible to slip through them. And while it isn't omnipotent or omniscient, it's also so far beyond humans that the residents of the CofD would never know it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T01:48:12-07:00","id":1075796,"title":"","content":"I am SOOOOOOOOOOO on-and-off about the damn God Machine. I think the Exarchs and Mage do Gnosticism much better than Demon and the GM do, and Dave Brookshaw has excised the GM and everything to do with it from the Mage core and has said on the forums that he personally doesn't even broach how the GM and Exarchs coexist. And even though that's not really argument enough against the God Machine, I have always been the kind of person who looks at something and when I see &quot;X game already exists and does this better&quot; it turns me off. But I acknowledge there are a hundred different arguments against that approach, chief of which being &quot;it may do this better for you but maybe not others&quot; but I've never seen any reason not to express my gaming opinions on a gaming forum, and hugely respect this thread.<br /> <br /> Tangent: it's a big reason I don't like Beast. I feel like Requiem does it a million times better and find it an enormous waste of time. I'd have no problem hearing the exact opposite argument made.<br /> <br /> BUT I do love Gnosticism so I can't help but love the GM sometimes. Also, Demon is about fucking -espionage- which makes it such a unique and fascinating concept in CofD. Also, this is a PERFECT place to rant about how I fell head over heels for Demon once I realized the whole thing was a send up to the role playing hobby as a whole, with the &quot;GM&quot; being the Game Master, the &quot;Infrastructure&quot; being the work put into the game, &quot;Angels&quot; being important NPCs, and &quot;Demons&quot; being PCs. The Agendas even line up with &quot;puzzle solvers&quot; &quot;in it for the loot&quot; &quot;thespian&quot; and &quot;risk takers.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's a work of genius, frankly.<br /> <br /> Still think Mage and Exarchs do &quot;gnosticism&quot; better. And I usually use the Principle and the Qashmallim for &quot;real&quot; Angels and Demons, and fly a massive middle finger at all the side bars that insist they are not actually God and the Angels, because I do what I want.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12981-romulusgloriosus","name":"RomulusGloriosus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"342"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T02:07:23-07:00","id":1075803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075796#post1075796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Still think Mage and Exarchs do &quot;gnosticism&quot; better. And I usually use the Principle and the Qashmallim for &quot;real&quot; Angels and Demons, and fly a massive middle finger at all the side bars that insist they are not actually God and the Angels, because I do what I want.</div> </div> </div> </div>Qashmallim do a nice job of filling the old, shit's-turned-real depictions of angels. Including the Satan-as-angel idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T05:02:49-07:00","id":1075839,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent#post1075671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bit of a tangent here, but the urge to post this has been bugging me for several days now. So I thought I'd get it over with and post my thoughts on the God Machine Chronicle.<br /> <br /> So I told myself I wouldn't be purchasing the<b> God Machine Chronicle</b> for reasons I will get to in a moment, but I've recently had little choice in the matter. With the Chronicles of Darkness moving its game lines onto second edition, I went ahead and bought the new rule book, along with Beast: the Primordial. My initial thoughts on the God Machine was that it was essentially the <b>World of Darkness: Matrix</b> edition, because everything I've heard come out of the game sounded like cyber-techno jargan. Infrastructure, embeds, codes, programs, glitches, radio signals. Everything sounded like the world was one big virtual simulation, but the people on Onyx Path insisted that this was not the case and that telling people it was the Matrix was unfair to the creators of the GMC<br /> <br /> So I decided to give the chronicle a read and I can say that I'm still not interested in it. From what I discovered after reading through the God Machine, it seems to be set in the realm of science fiction. Hell, there is even a quote near the start of the chapter that talks about how sufficiently advanced technology is indistinguishable from magic!<br /> <br /> When I bought WoD, I did so because it was a supernatural world set in the modern era. The God Machine Chronicle takes that world and tries to turn it into a <b>Shin Megami</b> spin off. If you think I'm exaggerating, there is actually an example scenario in the book that puts the fate of the world in humanity's hands. <i>The choices are eternal chaos, order, or free will</i>; the same possible choices you get to make at the end of Shin Megami when you choose to side with Demons, Angels, or Humanity! When I searched around online for the opinions of others who have played the game, one person told me that the GMC is basically an attempt to include a monotheistic deity into the game without offending any real world groups. And I've got to say I agree with that assessment.<br /> <br /> It is precisely because of its connection to GMC that I have no interest in ever buying <b>Demon: the Descent.</b> Which is disappointing, because I would normally find the idea of playing a demon to be pretty friggin metal. I just don't want to play a demon who's <i>actually made out of metal.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> I've come up with a simple solution for the problem, though. I simply ignore any and all references to the God Machine in my Chronicles of Darkness setting. If I want to incorporate a God, Demon or Angel into the story, I use <i>Spirits</i>, <i>Fey</i>, or similar creatures to substitute for them. It would not be hard to convince people that the seemingly omnipotent True Fey are deities, just as it would not be hard to use Ephemeral Beings to convince people of being demonic or angelic figures. So, to reiterate, the God Machine does not exist for me, nor do Angels and Demons as they are presented in that setting.<br /> <br /> <br /> -----------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry if that sounded like whining, or if it's already been said a hundred times; but I at least gave it a read. I will say, however, that before doing so, I hated the GMC because of my misconceptions about its premise. Now that I know more about it, my feelings have moved from hatred, to simply disinterest. I enjoy Shin Megami, I just don't feel like it needed a cross over with World of Darkness. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>And your solution is widely supported by the text. Golden Rule and all. Just bear something in mind: None of those scenarios are canonical, unless you include them in your chronicle. This isn't WoD, Chronicles of Darkness is plug &amp; play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T05:07:08-07:00","id":1075843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075790#post1075790\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Free Council would like to explain to you how wrong you are?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't checked out Mage, yet. I was thinking of getting it a while ago, but found out that Changeling 2E is coming out soon and decided to focus on that, instead. That being said, I'm still quite interested in picking it up and may get Mage 2e after Changeling. At this time, the only 2e books I have are Core and Beast. My Vampire and Werewolf books are still first edition. Having no books to go off of, my knowledge of Mage is extremely limited, but I was given to understand that Mages have the freedom to customize the way in which they channel and wield magic. One mage's casting style may be very different from another's, even if they are of the same Path. So while it is possible to have a faction of mages with close ties to technology, that does not mean every mage is of the same stock.<br /> <br /> In fact, I would describe such influences as being a form of casting fetish, rather than an actual form of magic.They're using technology and art to focus their minds and stave off Paradox, but such things are not inherently magical in and of themselves.<br /> <br /> <br /> But to anybody telling me that the other game lines deal with the idea of techno-magic science, or the God Machine, I already explained that I throw out any lore / mythology that involves the God Machine. That means across all the game lines, not just the core rule book. To me, the GMC is not a recognized part of the CoD lore; which is why I use other creatures from the mythos as substitutes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075839#post1075839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And your solution is widely supported by the text. Golden Rule and all. Just bear something in mind: None of those scenarios are canonical, unless you include them in your chronicle. This isn't WoD, Chronicles of Darkness is plug &amp; play.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, when I first got into WoD, I thought the world was set in stone by the books. It wasn't until I found these forums that I learned the rule books were more like friendly suggestions than a concrete setting. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075782#post1075782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> This is a very old argument that has plagued the fandom since the release of GMC. If you don't want to stir up old arguments, maybe don't make posts bringing up historically heated subjects. If you don't want to angrily bash GMC maybe don't start threads that have no point but to say &quot;here's why I don't like GMC.&quot; If you don't like it that's fine, but you don't need to publicly announce exactly why you don't like it to a bunch of people who do like it and are sick of defending it against exactly the same criticism for the past four years.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a new fan to White Wolf games. I didn't even know about their existence until Bloodlines came out, and by that point, the setting had gotten a reboot and moved onto second edition. So I'm like 20 something years late to the party on all this stuff, unfortunately. Bought my first edition books at a <i>Barnes and Noble </i>before I found out the books were no longer being marketed in print and my copies were outdated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-10-2017, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T06:03:02-07:00","id":1075849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075771#post1075771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1 - Because I was lead to believe that the monotheistic, non-machine deities can literally make their wills manifest. They don't need to carefully stack the dominos in place. If they want something to happen, it happens<br /> <br /> <br /> 2 - Yeah, I'm aware of that, but most of those who aren't omnipotent / omnipresent / omniscient are part of a collective pantheon, rather than being considered a singular individual. In my personal experience, monotheistic cultures tend to portray whatever deity they follow as being in control of everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even the Abrahamic God needed agents, both mortal and divine because humanity has free will.<br /> <br /> In fact, the central tension in a God Machine Chronicle is in fact, the machine's machinations to undo that free will, to the point that, when an angel develops one, they're excommunicated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T06:33:01-07:00","id":1075858,"title":"","content":"I'm also one of those guys that <i>really</i> wanted <b>DtD</b> to be their game - but then found out it was not very much my cup of cake. I even have Prestige Edition of <b>DtD</b> from Kickstarter on by bookshelf, even if I almost non used it ( checked only some 2E rules before getting other 2E corebooks few times ). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Still, even when I'm put off by this whole 'technological' aspect - I was first on our Polish Facebook group to point to mine CoDmate that <b>DtD</b> is <u>not</u> S-F - it's more like S-F/Horror or even S-F-Dark Fantasy ( if all CoD is treated as Dark Fantasy ). One and only real argument you need for it - <b>God Machine is about transforming <u>ESSENCE</u> in to other energy and powering it's Infrastructure.</b> And Essence is whole 'magical' energy of spirituality, in all it's variants However many technological steps or methods you are using later - you still operate on basically magical energy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T07:09:52-07:00","id":1075867,"title":"","content":"I am trying to keep the horse I have in this conflict safe, but I will say that separating science fiction and fantasy is, and remains, one of the things to be glad Victorian Britain is dead.<br /> <br /> When <i>fucking Tolkien</i> expounds greatly upon the metallurgy of Orcs and the obsession of Sauron with turning the world into his personal factory, it's time to maybe consider that tech has a place next to magic-perhaps even part of it, as Sauron is a literal fallen angel who sinned out of his desire to place tech and militant materialism over his own compassion. It's also worth remembering that Lovecraft's big thing was that &quot;sorcery&quot; is simply science not meant for human minds-sort of like the God-Machine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T07:56:43-07:00","id":1075883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075843#post1075843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm a new fan to White Wolf games. I didn't even know about their existence until Bloodlines came out, and by that point, the setting had gotten a reboot and moved onto second edition. So I'm like 20 something years late to the party on all this stuff, unfortunately. Bought my first edition books at a <i>Barnes and Noble </i>before I found out the books were no longer being marketed in print and my copies were outdated. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Bloodlines the computer game? That came out in 2004. About nine years before Chronicles of Darkness went to Second Edition. Anyway, your opening post makes it clear you've already come into contact with people defending GMC against this same old &quot;3scifi5me&quot; complaint. I'd think it would have been obvious that it's a hot button for a lot of folks here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T08:39:18-07:00","id":1075911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075883#post1075883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines the computer game? That came out in 2004. About nine years before Chronicles of Darkness went to Second Edition. Anyway, your opening post makes it clear you've already come into contact with people defending GMC against this same old &quot;3scifi5me&quot; complaint. I'd think it would have been obvious that it's a hot button for a lot of folks here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think by second edition he means NWoD rather than CWoD, not NWoDs transition into CoD and CoD 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T10:44:09-07:00","id":1075961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075883#post1075883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Bloodlines the computer game? That came out in 2004. About nine years before Chronicles of Darkness went to Second Edition. Anyway, your opening post makes it clear you've already come into contact with people defending GMC against this same old &quot;3scifi5me&quot; complaint. I'd think it would have been obvious that it's a hot button for a lot of folks here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Bloodlines drew my attention to the World of Darkness, but I didn't pick up any of the books until later, when I came across them in stores. I supposed the fact that B&amp;N only carried a single copy of each (mage, werewolf, vampire, core) should have tipped me off; but I went around looking for RP groups <i>after buying them</i> and found out the books had been out of print and nobody was using first edition. Which was a real let down for me, since I had basically wasted money on a version nobody was playing anymore. I still enjoyed the books anyways as inspirational source material for writing, however.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, Ashenrogue is correct. When I got here, <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> was still going by <b>New World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for the whole Tokein thing, I'm not a hard core tolkein fan. I've read The Hobbit, I watched the 'trilogy' that they somehow made out of a story that spanned a single book, and I watched the LotR trilogy that actually took place over the course of several books. But I do not remember any part explaining Sauron being an angel, or obsessing the details of orc craftsmanship. But I fail to see how that counters my idea on the subject. It's not the construction of the Orcs / Elves / Dwarves that's magical, it's the manner in which they are constructed that gives them their magical abilities. Anybody can forge a sword, piece of armor, or fine jewelry, but these races used some kind of supernatural crafting methods to give these creations unusual abilities. Likely some kind of <b>sympathetic magic</b> was used on their construction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T10:52:15-07:00","id":1075964,"title":"","content":"Too much here to comment on in its entirety, but I wanted to mention that I do wish the GMC content had included the corollary of Clarke's Law: &quot;Any sufficiently complex magic would be indistinguishable from technology.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T11:20:54-07:00","id":1075982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075961#post1075961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Bloodlines drew my attention to the World of Darkness, but I didn't pick up any of the books until later, when I came across them in stores. I supposed the fact that B&amp;N only carried a single copy of each (mage, werewolf, vampire, core) should have tipped me off; but I went around looking for RP groups <i>after buying them</i> and found out the books had been out of print and nobody was using first edition. Which was a real let down for me, since I had basically wasted money on a version nobody was playing anymore. I still enjoyed the books anyways as inspirational source material for writing, however.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, Ashenrogue is correct. When I got here, <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> was still going by <b>New World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for the whole Tokein thing, I'm not a hard core tolkein fan. I've read The Hobbit, I watched the 'trilogy' that they somehow made out of a story that spanned a single book, and I watched the LotR trilogy that actually took place over the course of several books. But I do not remember any part explaining Sauron being an angel, or obsessing the details of orc craftsmanship. But I fail to see how that counters my idea on the subject. It's not the construction of the Orcs / Elves / Dwarves that's magical, it's the manner in which they are constructed that gives them their magical abilities. Anybody can forge a sword, piece of armor, or fine jewelry, but these races used some kind of supernatural crafting methods to give these creations unusual abilities. Likely some kind of <b>sympathetic magic</b> was used on their construction.</div> </div> </div> </div>Silmarillion. Tolkein's own history of Middle-Earth. Goes on about how Sauron was one of the first blacksmiths of Middle-Earth, and ended up creating the Black Speech purely as a simplistic, easily-taught language that was meant to one day be the only language in all the world. And yes, his core motive was making all of the world a clockwork system of ruthless efficiency. In fact, that's one of the big divergences from the book-orcs are not barbarians, they're an advanced army (relatively) that cares only about getting from point A to point B as effectively as possible. Even their cannibalism is a reflection of this-it is simply more resources to them on the go, as it were.<br /> <br /> Also, Feanor. You want a perfect example of how hard it is to tell the difference between a mad sorcerer and a mad scientist, that elf is exhibit A, B, and C.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T12:03:06-07:00","id":1076017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RomulusGloriosus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075796#post1075796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am SOOOOOOOOOOO on-and-off about the damn God Machine. I think the Exarchs and Mage do Gnosticism much better than Demon and the GM do, and Dave Brookshaw has excised the GM and everything to do with it from the Mage core and has said on the forums that he personally doesn't even broach how the GM and Exarchs coexist.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you missed the point. So let's have a quick rewind. Note that this is from how I understand it and does not reflect on Brookshaw's actual opinions or choices.<br /> <br /> Around the time of Mage development, this entire argument concerning the God-Machine was going on. At the time, with the introduction of the Second Edition rules alongside it, one of the big prevailing worries that the God-Machine had gone from a cool bit of niche lore to an all consuming cornerstone. It didn't help that the God-Machine got a mention in Blood and Smoke(Requiem Second now) under the VII section as a possible origin for the 'covenant'. It was a problem.<br /> <br /> Mage, in the meanwhile, was designed to be a diver into the whole of the Chronicles world, that mages would explore every corner. That's a metric shit-ton of material to at least lightly touch on, and that's before you account that Mage itself has a wide amount of material to include and incorporate. As such, certain things needed to be left out. And since there was already plenty of attention/writing done on the G-M part of the world at that time, it was a pretty clear thing to ignore for the core book.<br /> <br /> I don't think Brookshaw's intention was to say &quot;The God-Machine is excised from Mage because problems&quot;-hell, Brookshaw was one of the big writers for The God-Machine Chronicle, and has stated his enjoyment of it a couple of times. The problem was that Mage was a stuffed book. You'll notice there's no mention of Changeling, the Strangers, or Arcadia either, and it's by and large for similar reasons.<br /> <br /> There probably also wasn't broaching it because the exact mechanical relationship between the Exarchs and the God-Machine are best defined at individual tables in the spirit of solving mysteries and becoming Mysteries than providing some kind of definitive answer. It works out, because I've seen Brookshaw's headcanon on that(it's here on the forums somewhere) and while it's cool, I wouldn't run it that way.<br /> <br /> Mage will cover the God-Machine and Descent as surely as it will make a Mystery out of cArcadia and Lost eventually, but the core needed a better focus on the things that would matter most to Mage, that's were much more immediate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T12:13:15-07:00","id":1076027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076017#post1076017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I don't think Brookshaw's intention was to say &quot;The God-Machine is excised from Mage because problems&quot;-hell, Brookshaw was one of the big writers for The God-Machine Chronicle, and has stated his enjoyment of it a couple of times. The problem was that Mage was a stuffed book. You'll notice there's no mention of Changeling, the Strangers, or Arcadia either, and it's by and large for similar reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I thought Mage intentionally left it ambiguous as to whether or not Mage Arcadia and Changeling Arcadia were one in the same. So it was ultimately up to the players to decide how they wanted to treat it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T12:21:41-07:00","id":1076035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076027#post1076027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I thought Mage intentionally left it ambiguous as to whether or not Mage Arcadia and Changeling Arcadia were one in the same. So it was ultimately up to the players to decide how they wanted to treat it.</div> </div> </div> </div>In text, it hasn't happened yet, but it has been answered because both sides are tired of the shit: the Arcadias aren't the same as far as canon is concerned. Fans can make the connection, but the plans for the books involve dropping the issue completely.<br /> <br /> This has been stated a couple of times on the forums since 2013.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T12:29:30-07:00","id":1076046,"title":"","content":"Worth mentioning that, while I don't know if this is the case or not, had there not been the problem of introducing Goetia in this game and angels could fill in their usual spot in the triad of Ephemeral Beings, there probably would have been more mention of the G-M's fuckery. But since Goetia and Supernal/Abyssal beings really needed in, angels weren't covered, and it probably made more sense to keep the focus in-house from there.<br /> <br /> Like, again, Mage is stuffed book. They barely managed to get one Legacy in there, a lot of special rules got hyper condensed for Mage's particular enemies, just-It was a <i>crammed</i> book. You can't cover every inch of reality in that same book, even in passing, and the God-Machine has a rather substantial amount of real-estate to cover from a Mage writing perspective. Easier to just move on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T12:45:27-07:00","id":1076051,"title":"","content":"Years ago, when it was still new, I stumbled across Mage: The Ascension and while I found the whole concept of Conceptual Reality fascinating it didn't feel like magic to me so I skipped the game. Two decades later I run into Mage: The Awakening on the subnet while searching for game ideas for Vampire and I'm hooked. This felt like magic and the supernatural again. Sure it's all fluff and you can dress the game up anyway you like but it's that fluff that catches the eye long enough to learn the mechanics.<br /> \u200bOn the same front the idea of playing sentient machines trapped in a cold war doesn't appeal to me so I haven't bought the book, not even after scanning what was on the subnet (which had been enough to get me to buy both Werewolf and Mage, I had just decided to buy Changeling when I found out a 2ed was coming and decided to wait).<br /> \u200bI have however used God-Machine Infrastructure in a Mage story. I tried to give it a Lovecraft feel, with unknown origins and purpose but my 'villains' had repurposed it for their own murderous plans.<br /> \u200bNothing to do with how well it's written or if it's a good concept, some things just don't appeal to me.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for religion in Role Play, I just go with the idea that faith (any faith) has power, primarily in how it motivates people, and leave questions of what is true to the real world, it's not needed at the game table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T12:50:53-07:00","id":1076054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knowbody</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075964#post1075964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Too much here to comment on in its entirety, but I wanted to mention that I do wish the GMC content had included the corollary of Clarke's Law: &amp;quot;Any sufficiently complex magic would be indistinguishable from technology.&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that's not genuine Clarke. It also decidedly misses the point of Clarke's Third, which as mentioned above, is an observation about the scientific process. This hypothetical corollary assumes the possibility of magic that is distinct from science, which is simply put not how science works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T13:11:24-07:00","id":1076063,"title":"","content":"Relevant quotes to what I was talking about<b></b>:<br /> <br /> <u><b>God-Machine and Mage</b></u><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/392-addicted-to-mystery-what-do-you-want-to-see-in-the-fallen-world-chronicles?p=121125#post121125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I *like* the God-Machine. I think it's awesome. I dropped hints toward it in earlier sourcebooks (like many people did), wrote for the GMC Anthology, was the less-outspoken third of the rules team working on the new nWoD engine, wrote for Demon, wrote for the Demon Player's Guide, and am writing for the Demon Anthology. I enjoy the mythology.<br /> <br /> I'm still not going to put any God-Machine references in Mage. We don't need more setting elements. We have setting elements coming out of our <i>ears</i>. Ghost Mages, Genius Locii, and Temple Guardians have still never been expanded on. Two years ago, the Mad, Scelesti, and Tremere would have been on the list, too.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/324537-2nd-edition-weekly-discussion-the-onmyodo-mage-in-tokyo?p=326487#post326487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Essentially, we just don't have room for a crossover section or we would, indeed, have &quot;how to treat the other gamelines as Mysteries&quot;. Maybe it'll find itself a home in a future book, the way the Demon Storyteller's Guide is going to? The last time <b>Mage</b> looked at the other games was in Tome of the Mysteries, when half of them weren't out.</div> </div> </div> </div><u><b>Faerie and Mage</b></u><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/413769-the-cosmology-of-the-new-world-of-darkness?p=415028#post415028\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In first edition, it was up in the air, but in second edition our decision to make the Supernal World what you see when using Mage Sight, and the Supernal <i>Realms</i> the unseen Supernal without the shape of the world to give it structure, has made it much clearer. The Supernal isn't a physical place, it <i>is</i> a conceptual space, and this has a few other knock-on effects; first ed Geist and Changeling flirted (changeling much more so) that Stygia and Mage Arcadia were in the Underworld and Changeling Arcadia.<br /> <br /> They're not. As of second edition, the &quot;Arcadia Question&quot; is answered with a great big No. The things that abduct people through the Hedge are not Supernal Fae, any more than the fuel Demons use is the Supernal World of the Obrimos. We considered the ramifications carefully, and decided that a long-teased crossover issue was an acceptable loss for the setting change we wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dave Brookshaw</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/697367-god-machine-and-divine-fire-in-mage-centric-cosmology?p=702470#post702470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The quality a Lower Depth lacks doesn't have to map exactly to one of the Arcana - the Strix hunger for life, but Vitae isn't &quot;The Life Arcanum,&quot; not exactly. Inferno demons are drawn to sin and cruelty.<br /> <br /> The Gentry are beings of story that have a desperate need to both follow narrative themselves and force others to. By explicitly splitting Changeling's cosmology off from Supernal Arcadia, we can look at that straight-on should we decide to do a crossover. What does the interaction of a splat whose powers are based on symbolism and beings who are living stories look like?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There's more, but I don't wanna bog down the thread or distract more from the central conflict. Still, thought some context would be appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T13:20:20-07:00","id":1076068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1075858#post1075858\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>God Machine is about transforming <u>ESSENCE</u> in to other energy and powering it's Infrastructure.</b> And Essence is whole 'magical' energy of spirituality, in all it's variants However many technological steps or methods you are using later - you still operate on basically magical energy.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, Shadowrun draws a clear distinction between magic and technology. While both exist within the same world as each other, they are not the same thing. In fact, the more ingrained you are to the technical side of things, the less adept at magic you are. Adapting your body with artificial implants diminishes your Essence and (if you aren't careful) will eventually reduce you to a soulless husk of your former self.<br /> <br /> That's basically the kind of approach that I like to think of when addressing the issue of magic vs science. I would allow for magic and technology to exist within the same world as each other, but I also want them to be completely separate from one another.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076051#post1076051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bNothing to do with how well it's written or if it's a good concept, some things just don't appeal to me.<br /> <br /> \u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Same for me. I'm not saying the God Machine was poorly written or planned out. I just don't care for the mythos surrounding it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-10-2017, 04:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T13:41:34-07:00","id":1076078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076054#post1076054\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure that's not genuine Clarke. It also decidedly misses the point of Clarke's Third, which as mentioned above, is an observation about the scientific process. This hypothetical corollary assumes the possibility of magic that is distinct from science, which is simply put not how science works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I'm aware it's not actually Clarke (pretty sure it's from Mercedes Lackey, but I'd have to check to be sure), but it is a line that makes me smile and in some ways suits the nature of the God-Machine just as well as the oft-referenced Clarke's First Law. Infrastructure doesn't necessarily take the form of massive gears and circuits, after all; it's been stated numerous times both in the books and here on the forums that the GM is the sum total of all occult matrices/infrastructure/what have you in existence. That applies equally to a blood sacrifice in an ancient ring of standing stones as to a factory that renders human souls down into fuel for biomechanical angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/747-knowbody","name":"Knowbody","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T14:49:25-07:00","id":1076130,"title":"","content":"Admittedly this is only partially relevant, but to elaborate a little bit on what Leliel said before about Lovecraftian &quot;sorcery as hyper-technology&quot;, there has been an effort in late years to reconcile the tech aspect of the Cthulhu Mythos with the horror one. Not as in, &quot;sci-fi tech weird aliens use and that we can grab&quot; but more like &quot;I absolutely have no idea how this works and is so removed from my conception of the laws of reality <i>it is </i>magic for me&quot;.<br /> <br /> It all relates to the fact 80 years of pop-cultural osmosis kinda deprived the Cthulhu Mythos of the sense of mind-melting revelations that are at the core of the Cosmic Horror genre.<br /> <br /> Alongside that, there's this little heresy which I appreciate a lot that's all about what happens when Gnosticism meets Lovecraft. Curiously, the two currents coexists. Dark Gnosticims enable by science so advanced only an enlightened (read: broken but now wise) mind can comprehend. Advanced technology has a place in horror today more than ever. It fits the zeitgeist.<br /> <br /> I know that many people here disagree (even a couple of notable ones, like some Demon writers and such) but the God-Machine <i>is </i>Cosmic Horror. Sure, it does not meets all the points of the &quot;Lovecraft's checklist for Cosmic Horror&quot; but, listen to this crazy idea, that's because it's done by people that <i>know what they're doing</i>. You can do Lovecraftian homages in thousands of way, and the examples of people that pick the superficial aspects of the Cthulhu Mythos for their work are countless. They can be good, they can be bad, nothing intrinsecally wrong with that. I do the same, sometimes.<br /> <br /> But to create something new, fresh, and that works, you've got to pick certain aspects of the genre, discard others and, perhaps most importantly, burn some others down and scatter the ashes. You can do that by having a deep understanding both of the tropes of the genre and of narrative in general. God-Machine and Demon do that. Bloodborne does too (seriously, I can write pages explaining how that game is utterly devote and beneficial to Lovecraft while departing from many core elements of H.P.'s works)<br /> <br /> It's not deconstruction nor reconstruction. It's an evolution and the existence of these is a good thing all around. You can improve the Cosmic Horror genre as a whole by looking at works like this.<br /> <br /> Now, I do believe the authors were fully aware of what they were writing (they're a smart bunch of people) but, conscious or not, the elements that give the God-Machine and Demon their personality don't deprive them of their bite.<br /> <br /> It would be a disservice to say that the techgnostic elements of Demon are mere aesthetic, but it's also true that to focus on them while not giving a chance to the whole picture under the mechanical surface is like looking at the finger instead of looking at the moon.<br /> <br /> If you still don't like it afterwards, it's perfectly fine, but Demon is not about &quot;Matrix robots fighting the system&quot; just like Changeling is not &quot;5 Stages of grief: The Game&quot; and Beast is not &quot;1001 ways to justify abuse&quot;. There will always be people that will describe the game as that, but that's objectively not true.<br /> <br /> Or at least, there's more than that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 04-12-2017, 06:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:07:47-07:00","id":1076135,"title":"","content":"I actually quite liked the mechanical aspect, but I wanted more abrahamic interpretations for my specific world. I sidestepped with good ol' fashioned Gnosticism and Alchemy. I'd say Mage is more similar to The Matrix than GMC is. I didn't really like the GM that much at first either, but it has grown on me a little. I just have to mold it to fit into my setting. I could of course have not used it but I thought there were enough good ideas that it would be a shame to waste, though people here seem a bit jugey about wanting to use abrahamic and renaissance style Angels and Demons. I don't know what is up with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:20:31-07:00","id":1076146,"title":"","content":"Say, Nyrufa, remember how you said in the Beast forums how you didn't understand what was the controversy with Beast?<br /> <br /> That controversy was due to people perceiving Beast a game about playing sadistic abusers and justifying it. <br /> <br /> Now, was that assessment entirely wrong? Well, it has some grounds in truth. And that's why it's so insidious- it is a shallow reading that focuses on the most edgy bits instead of the deeper Whys and Hows in the game, and forms a first impression of the game that is detrimental to understanding the game in its entirety. It's a vicious cycle where people never look past the surface because all they looked at was the surface. <br /> <br /> That is exactly what's happening with this re-open debate. And why everyone, including me, is obssessed on 'correcting' you. Not that we have any chance or right to change your preferences, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:28:55-07:00","id":1076151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076130#post1076130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It all relates to the fact 80 years of pop-cultural osmosis kinda deprived the Cthulhu Mythos of the sense of mind-melting revelations that are at the core of the Cosmic Horror genre.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The idea of cosmic horror isn't about highly advanced beings that mind blast us the second we see them. It's the idea that these creatures are so far beyond our comprehension that there is absolutely nothing we can do to fight them. Once you give their victims some capacity to rebel against their machinations, no matter how small, you take away the spirit of the Lovecraft mythos. That's why Call of Cthulhu doesn't really work from an action stand point. If you can load up a rifle and start blowing away Deep Ones and Shuggoths, then they stop being scary. They're not ancient, cosmic horrors, they're just a bunch of ugly aliens who need to be driven off the planet. There's a reason why so many people in the Lovecraft stories end up in a mental institution; and not, say, the armed forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-10-2017, 07:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:30:37-07:00","id":1076152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076151#post1076151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The idea of cosmic horror isn't about highly advanced beings that mind blast us the second we see them. It's the idea that these creatures are so far beyond our comprehension that there is absolutely nothing we can do to fight them. Once you give their victims some capacity to rebel against their machinations, no matter how small, you take away the spirit of the Lovecraft mythos. That's why Call of Cthulhu doesn't really work from an action stand point. If you can load up a rifle and start blowing away Deep Ones and Shuggoths, then they stop being scary. They're not ancient, cosmic horrors, they're just a bunch of ugly aliens who need to be driven off the planet. There's a reason why so many people in the Lovecraft stories end up in a mental institution; and not, say, the armed forced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, would you consider crashing a boat into one as fighting back a little bit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:42:28-07:00","id":1076159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076146#post1076146\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Say, Nyrufa, remember how you said in the Beast forums how you didn't understand what was the controversy with Beast?<br /> <br /> That controversy was due to people perceiving Beast a game about playing sadistic abusers and justifying it.<br /> <br /> Now, was that assessment entirely wrong? Well, it has some grounds in truth. And that's why it's so insidious- it is a shallow reading that focuses on the most edgy bits instead of the deeper Whys and Hows in the game, and forms a first impression of the game that is detrimental to understanding the game in its entirety. It's a vicious cycle where people never look past the surface because all they looked at was the surface.<br /> <br /> That is exactly what's happening with this re-open debate. And why everyone, including me, is obssessed on 'correcting' you. Not that we have any chance or right to change your preferences, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>I recently had an epiphany in regards to how the God Machine's technology can be similar to my brand of magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Radio Signals = Incantations<br /> <br /> Circuitry = Leylines<br /> <br /> Infrastructure = Glyphs , Runes, Wards<br /> <br /> <br /> Probably some other comparisons, but they've slipped my mind now. Anyways, the point is that I can see from a scientific stand point how the GM can be interpreted as magical. <i>However, I personally do not accept it as such.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I am not trying to disuade people from using the God Machine if that is what they want to do. It's their game, go for it. I am explaining why I personally choose not to do so. I have not and never will consider magic to be technological in nature. I consider it to be its own, independent force with capabilities that defy scientific understanding. For me, casting a fireball is not a mage increasing the friction in the air to ignite a spark in the environment. It is the mage conjuring flames out of nothing and manipulating it through their force of will. It doesn't need fuel to burn, but rather it burns because the mage wants it to burn.<br /> <br /> <i>That is my stance on magic.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076152#post1076152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Well, would you consider crashing a boat into one as fighting back a little bit?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Depends on how the creature reacts. If you draw blood and make it yell in pain? Then yeah, that would be fighting back. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If the creature just tanks the vehicle without batting an eye in your direction, then no.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T15:56:15-07:00","id":1076166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076151#post1076151\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The idea of cosmic horror isn't about highly advanced beings that mind blast us the second we see them. It's the idea that these creatures are so far beyond our comprehension that there is absolutely nothing we can do to fight them. Once you give their victims some capacity to rebel against their machinations, no matter how small, you take away the spirit of the Lovecraft mythos. That's why Call of Cthulhu doesn't really work from an action stand point. If you can load up a rifle and start blowing away Deep Ones and Shuggoths, then they stop being scary. They're not ancient, cosmic horrors, they're just a bunch of ugly aliens who need to be driven off the planet. There's a reason why so many people in the Lovecraft stories end up in a mental institution; and not, say, the armed forced.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember when I said there are departure points? Here you go. Demons can fight the Angels (who says they can defeat the God-Machine though?) and in Bloodborne you cut Great Old Ones down. Not a big deal, as I already explained.<br /> <br /> Science and &quot;eldritch abominations from the stygian depths beyond the walls of the safe haven we call sanity&quot; can coexist. It's the scale that matters. The Mythos are scientific. Utterly, unequivocally scientific. If the many examples in the story themselves are not enough (like summoning Nyarlathotep with advanced mathematics or the Great Race that exchanges minds through a combination of machinery and telepathy, to cite a couple) they are scientific by Lovecraft's own admission. There are countless letters where he states he wrote them to be that way. Lovecraft himself states that highly-advanced beings and gods behind our comprehension are the same thing in his works. I could go scavenge for quotes but I already write about Lovecraft enough for my college thesis.<br /> <br /> Fighting back? Plenty of people fight back. The notion you can't it's more memetic than factual.Curwen dies. Wilbur and his brother are kicked in their tentacled butt and defeated. At the end of the icy Kadath, Nyarlathotep loses. It's all about the scale and the fact that when you start to realize the nightmarish reality of the whole picture you have good chances to lose your mind because in the end you, those you care about and your life don't matter.<br /> <br /> In Demon though? You get Angels that hurl galaxies at each other and yet you still have the chance to carve your own Hell. Cosmic Horror with shades of hope. Variations of the recipe that have a truly good reason to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 04-10-2017, 07:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T16:18:35-07:00","id":1076173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076159#post1076159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I recently had an epiphany in regards to how the God Machine's technology can be similar to my brand of magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Radio Signals = Incantations<br /> <br /> Circuitry = Leylines<br /> <br /> Infrastructure = Glyphs , Runes, Wards<br /> <br /> <br /> Probably some other comparisons, but they've slipped my mind now. Anyways, the point is that I can see from a scientific stand point how the GM can be interpreted as magical.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Precisely</b>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>However, I personally do not accept it as such.</i><br /> <br /> I am not trying to disuade people from using the God Machine if that is what they want to do. It's their game, go for it. I am explaining why I personally choose not to do so. I have not and never will consider magic to be technological in nature. I consider it to be its own, independent force with capabilities that defy scientific understanding. For me, casting a fireball is not a mage increasing the friction in the air to ignite a spark in the environment. It is the mage conjuring flames out of nothing and manipulating it through their force of will. It doesn't need fuel to burn, but rather it burns because the mage wants it to burn.<br /> <br /> <i>That is my stance on magic.</i> </div> </div> </div>And we finally reached some sort of agreement, it seems. I have a feeling that you love Changeling and Beast <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (Ironically enough, Mage itself has its brand of magic analyzable and measurable. Under a strict restriction that it has to be a non-Sleeper doing the science. Hell, there's even someone who Ascended by studying how particles collide, but observing all that with Mage Sight)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T16:33:39-07:00","id":1076178,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076159#post1076159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I recently had an epiphany in regards to how the God Machine's technology can be similar to my brand of magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Radio Signals = Incantations<br /> <br /> Circuitry = Leylines<br /> <br /> Infrastructure = Glyphs , Runes, Wards<br /> <br /> <br /> Probably some other comparisons, but they've slipped my mind now. Anyways, the point is that I can see from a scientific stand point how the GM can be interpreted as magical. <i>However, I personally do not accept it as such.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Also remember that the GM doesn't just operate through technology, it does things like get cults to do rituals and perform sacrifices in the right spot on the right days.<br /> <br /> Sure there might be a device which has the circuits (which are made from the planetary metals) arranged to be an array of occult diagrams which when turned on will construct an angel to hunt down the demons which have been corrupting the local government with pacts and tempting them to sin, but that machine is likely to be powered by a cult three blocks away called the Order of Astaroth, who have to perform the rite of fourteen hearts where fourteen dedicated cultists make small cuts on their foreheads while the rest of the priests recite the tale of Saint Jeremiah from their sacred text. And then once it has been successful and a new glorious angel is conjured, the next day the statue of astaroth begins to bleed aether from his own forehead.<br /> <br /> Now, you don't like the tech side, but it's easy to remove, not just from GMC but Demon the Descent itself. The only tech aspects in it are really the Demon Form abilities (nearly all of which also give a description of how it would look for a traditional abrahamic demon/angel so just only use the non-tech descriptions), and that exploit gadgets look sci-fi (which even in my own games, I change to look infernal rather than sci-fi).<br /> <br /> The God-Machine is a machine not because it's technological, but because of it operates. It is a massive confusing apparatus, each part of which has it's own purpose and it tries to get those parts to achieve their purpose by getting them to work together. It is the &quot;God works in mysterious ways&quot;, doing hundreds of little actions in the background to achieve a set output. <br /> <br /> In addition, the God-Machine has technological aspects for three reasons.<br /> First so that it can be omnipresent and omniscient, without the game immediately breaking. Technology is everywhere, it tracks your life, everything you do is noted by the system. The only way to escape it would be to leave places with technology all together, but remember that technology is not just wires, cameras, and hard drives. Paper is a technology. Stone carvings are a technology. To escape technology is possible, but still difficult enough for the GM to remain effectively omnipresent.<br /> <br /> The second reason is so that it is alien. So that it isn't &quot;God&quot;. By being technological, it has a sense of the other it is something that doesn't match the myths of man. It is grander than man's understanding of deities or the universe. The God-Machine is a demiurge, it may be maintaining gravity, giving people holy missions, and controlling armies of angels, but it is not the true creator. Admittedly, this aspect is sometimes disliked. <br /> <br /> Finally, it is technological because if a deity does exist, than it's creations and actions aren't magic. They are physics. If the stars were made by deities, those stars aren't magic, they are part of the natural state of the world because the deities have willed it so. If gravity exists because of deities, then they aren't doing a spell to keep it there, gravity would exist because the deities say it should exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 04-10-2017, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T16:40:42-07:00","id":1076181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076173#post1076173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>Precisely</b>.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And we finally reached some sort of agreement, it seems. I have a feeling that you love Changeling and Beast <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At this moment, <b>Changeling: the Lost</b> is probably my favorite of the Chronicles of Darkness lines; and I don't even own the book, yet!<br /> <br /> <br /> Ironically, <b>Changeling: the Dreaming</b> is probably my least favorite of the World of Darkness lines, because the entire setting is downright depressing. Good job, White Wolf, your made a game I can empathize with! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-10-2017, 07:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T16:51:21-07:00","id":1076183,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1394_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1394\" data-vbnamecard=\"1394\">Nyrufa</a> how about making it explode into green mist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T17:32:19-07:00","id":1076197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076159#post1076159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not trying to disuade people from using the God Machine if that is what they want to do. It's their game, go for it. I am explaining why I personally choose not to do so. I have not and never will consider magic to be technological in nature. I consider it to be its own, independent force with capabilities that defy scientific understanding. For me, casting a fireball is not a mage increasing the friction in the air to ignite a spark in the environment. It is the mage conjuring flames out of nothing and manipulating it through their force of will. It doesn't need fuel to burn, but rather it burns because the mage wants it to burn.<br /> <br /> <i>That is my stance on magic.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>This seems like a statement you should make to your fellow players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T18:23:59-07:00","id":1076223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076159#post1076159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not trying to disuade people from using the God Machine if that is what they want to do. It's their game, go for it. I am explaining why I personally choose not to do so. I have not and never will consider magic to be technological in nature. I consider it to be its own, independent force with capabilities that defy scientific understanding. For me, casting a fireball is not a mage increasing the friction in the air to ignite a spark in the environment. It is the mage conjuring flames out of nothing and manipulating it through their force of will. It doesn't need fuel to burn, but rather it burns because the mage wants it to burn.<br /> <br /> <i>That is my stance on magic.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Of course, if that mage recasts and studies their Fireball, seeking to quantify how hot it gets, and/or how they can improve their casting by understanding the details, that is still science again. And if they apply that knowledge, we are back to technology...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T18:37:24-07:00","id":1076231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076223#post1076223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course, if that mage recasts and studies their Fireball, seeking to quantify how hot it gets, and/or how they can improve their casting by understanding the details, that is still science again. And if they apply that knowledge, we are back to technology...</div> </div> </div> </div>This. If something can provably be done in violation of the laws of physics (like, for example, creating fire with no catalyst that burns with no fuel), a good scientist doesnt state dumbfounded and protest &quot;but that's against the <i>rules</i>!&quot; A good scientist asks &quot;how was my understanding of the laws of physics wrong?&quot; If fuelless fire can be made by repeatable processes, it doesn't matter if those processes fit within the current understanding of science, science will adapt to account for this new possibility. Because science isn't a system of rules, it's a process of explaining how things work.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T18:39:48-07:00","id":1076232,"title":"","content":"Perhaps a better corollary for Clarke's Third Law would be &quot;any sufficiently understood magic is indistinguishable from technology.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T19:18:33-07:00","id":1076240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076223#post1076223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Of course, if that mage recasts and studies their Fireball, seeking to quantify how hot it gets, and/or how they can improve their casting by understanding the details, that is still science again. And if they apply that knowledge, we are back to technology...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> No, because again; the fire isn't operating under the boundaries of scientific observation. The fire is behaving in the fashion that it does simply because the mage in question wants the fire to do so. They will the fire to burn hotter, so it burns hotter, they will the fire to burn without fuel, so it burns without fuel, they will it to hold a specific shape or consistency, est. It's impossible to quantify, because it's only limitations are those of the mage's own imagination and personal training.<br /> <br /> They could use science and technology in order to <b><i>simulate the spell</i>,</b> but it would not be the same thing as actually using magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Take Dungeons and Dragons, for example. The spell &quot;Burning Hands&quot; allows the mage to expel a cone of flames from their hands. Now I could, in theory, strap a portable flame thrower to my wrists and shoot fire in that way. But I'm not casting Burning Hands, I'm using a machine to <i><b>simulate</b></i> the casting of Burning Hands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-10-2017, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T19:25:01-07:00","id":1076241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076240#post1076240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, because again; the fire isn't operating under the boundaries of scientific observation. The fire is behaving in the fashion that it does simply because the mage in question wants the fire to do so. They will the fire to burn hotter, so it burns hotter, they will the fire to burn without fuel, so it burns without fuel, they will it to hold a specific shape or consistency, est. It's impossible to quantify, because it's only limitations are those of the mage's own imagination and personal training.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you're describing is science. The mage is aware of what it takes to make the fire, and they use their will and Supernal symbology to bring it about instead of flint and steel.<br /> <br /> The only way you're getting away from science in mage is if you work solely with Abyssal magic.<br /> <br /> Supernal magic has rules, those rules are science, gained through experimentation and observation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T19:28:45-07:00","id":1076243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076240#post1076240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> No, because again; the fire isn't operating under the boundaries of scientific observation. The fire is behaving in the fashion that it does simply because the mage in question wants the fire to do so. They will the fire to burn hotter, so it burns hotter, they will the fire to burn without fuel, so it burns without fuel, they will it to hold a specific shape or consistency, est. It's impossible to quantify, because it's only limitations are those of the mage's own imagination and personal training.<br /> <br /> They could use science and technology in order to <b><i>simulate the spell</i>,</b> but it would not be the same thing as actually using magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Take Dungeons and Dragons, for example. The spell &quot;Burning Hands&quot; allows the mage to expel a cone of flames from their hands. Now I could, in theory, strap a portable flame thrower to my wrists and shoot fire in that way. But I'm not casting Burning Hands, I'm using a machine to <i><b>simulate</b></i> the casting of Burning Hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't talking about trying to copy spells with mechanical devices. If a mage can create fire with their mind, that's technology. If the mage can repeat the event by creating fire with their mind again, you can apply scientific process to it and study it. Because if something can happen, it isn't magic by definition. You can call it magic, but the second it exists then things happened to make it exist. It's just might be using laws we don't understand yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T19:32:42-07:00","id":1076244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076241#post1076241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What you're describing is science. The mage is aware of what it takes to make the fire, and they use their will and Supernal symbology to bring it about instead of flint and steel.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> But how do you quantify Will and Symbology? I'm pretty sure that the scientific community doesn't accept the claim<b> &quot;this works because I believe that it works&quot;</b> when attempting to explain something. Science demands evidence and proof, not outstanding claims and baseless speculation. That very mage (or even another one, entirely) could turn around and say <b>&quot;now I believe that it doesn't work!&quot;</b> It is for that reason that Will Working and Hard Science can not mutually exist. By their very definitions, they cancel each other out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-10-2017, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T19:39:55-07:00","id":1076246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076244#post1076244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how do you quantify Will and Symbology? I'm pretty sure that the scientific community doesn't accept the claim &quot;this works because I believe that it works&quot; when attempting to explain something.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not how magic works, either. But semiotics is a science. Neuroscience is a science. They have machines, including ambulatory limbs, that are controlled by thought. There is no difference between that and what mages do except people don't have access to a Supernal world.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Science demands evidence and proof, not outstanding claims and baseless speculation. It is for that reason that Will Working and Hard Science can not mutually exist. By their very definitions, they cancel each other out. </div> </div> </div>That's nonsense and, as noted, it's why there's something called the Free Council. Supernal magic exists alongside 'hard science' very well. The mortal scientific community doesn't have to agree to it existing for it to work, consensual reality, or consensual fantasy, is not a thing. We have astronomers despite flat earth theory. We have marine biologists despite communities that have never seen the ocean. We have historians, archaeologists and anthropologists despite factions of people believing the world isn't more than 4-6 thousand years old.<br /> <br /> The moment two Awakened got together and said, 'Look what I can do' they had evidence and proof.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T19:44:02-07:00","id":1076249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076244#post1076244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> But how do you quantify Will and Symbology? I'm pretty sure that the scientific community doesn't accept the claim &quot;this works because I believe that it works&quot; when attempting to explain something. Science demands evidence and proof, not outstanding claims and baseless speculation. It is for that reason that Will Working and Hard Science can not mutually exist. By their very definitions, they cancel each other out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well you can travel to the inside of the mages Mind/Soul and record the data of their will and what symbols their souls are producing. You can actually give non-mages the ability to see the symbols with their own eyes. You could take people into the willworkers mind. Etc.<br /> <br /> And that's before getting to the fact that despite the fact that I cannot see atoms with my naked eyes, scientists are reasonably sure they exist.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":8331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","user":"milo v3","date":". 04-10-2017, 10:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T19:54:10-07:00","id":1076250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076246#post1076246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's not how magic works, either.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's how MY version of magic works; which is the point I have been trying to clarify from the start of this discussion.<br /> <br /> In MY version of magic; it can not be quantified or studied because the variables are ever changing. Magic functions in the manner that is presented because the mage using it wants the magic to function in that fashion. It has nothing to do with scientific reasoning or physics. It's concentrated desire forced upon the world. Anybody with a comparably strong willpower or opposing desire could effectively cancel out their magic. Not because of the nature of opposing forces, but simply because they wanted their desired outcome more strongly than their opponent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-10-2017, 11:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T19:57:13-07:00","id":1076252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076250#post1076250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's how MY version of magic works; which is the point I have been trying to clarify from the start of this discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Does your version of magic have any limits or rules? Looks like &quot;will&quot; is at least one. Others?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T20:00:07-07:00","id":1076255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076250#post1076250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's how MY version of magic works; which is the point I have been trying to clarify from the start of this discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't really matter since his post (and mine) specifically still are applicable to the magic you have described.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T20:04:36-07:00","id":1076256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076250#post1076250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's how MY version of magic works; which is the point I have been trying to clarify from the start of this discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and I've been pointing out that if there's rules to it, even if you tie them to hard to quantify things like souls and willpower, that's still science. It's still cause and effect.<br /> <br /> The magic that gets away from all that is in other games, or the Abyss, but the Supernal mages of Awakening are probably the most scientifically-minded magicians, to the point they've even defined the limits of their arcana at different levels through the Practices, understanding how Reach and yantra work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T20:14:23-07:00","id":1076258,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076252#post1076252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does your version of magic have any limits or rules? Looks like &quot;will&quot; is at least one. Others?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Actually, yeah. The way I view magic is that when two or more magic users clash, it's not a matter of opposing forces, but rather a contest of willpower. A mage's spells are only as strong as the willpower behind them. A defensive mage who allows their focus to waver can have their defenses penetrated. Regardless if they're trying to block an oncoming fire spell with a wall of smothering dirt, or a zone of pure oxygen.<br /> <br /> <br /> Likewise, I also use the rule that a mage's magic can be developed through constant practice; but this is once again due to the power of their belief. They have cast the spell enough times in the past that they are confident they can do so again when they need to. Attempting to cast a brand new spell, especially one that is being improvised in the heat of the moment is technically possible, but it may not be as potent because the magic user is having personal doubts about their abilities. This also is used to explain why the most powerful spells are so difficult to cast. There's not a whole lot of opportunity to practice them; so there aren't any real experts on their usage. You don't whip out a nuclear bomb as casually as a hand grenade, you save it as a last resort.<br /> <br /> <br /> When it comes to casting magic, any use of incantations, spell components, symbols and the like are essentially a placebo effect. By themselves, they do not give the mage any actual power. But the Mage can trick themselves into believing that they do, in order to make it easier to cast their spells or to improve their effectiveness. This would also be used to explain why normal people or the undisciplined can not wield such artifacts properly. They don't have the proper experience to focus their minds; so it seems like the artifact is worthless to them, or that is functions improperly from its intended purpose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-10-2017, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T20:23:49-07:00","id":1076263,"title":"","content":"Have you tried Mage the Ascension?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T20:29:44-07:00","id":1076264,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076263#post1076263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you tried Mage the Ascension?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I have not; and I know virtually nothing about it. From what I tried reading, it sounded like another attempt at techno-magic (that's what came to mind when I read the term 'technocracy') and I lost interest in it for the same reason I lost interest in God Machine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T20:37:12-07:00","id":1076265,"title":"","content":"Alright, look, all science is is a way of observing the world. That's it. If something can be observed and repeated then it can be studied scientifically. It can be quantified. If magic cannot be observed and cannot be repeated then there is simply no way it can work.<br /> If a scientist sees someone shooting fire from their hands, their first reaction is not &quot;nope, that's impossible&quot; it's &quot;how does that work? Willpower you say? Can you do it again so I can measure how hot it is? Now can you do it in front of these sensors so I can see if it needs fuel like normal fire? It doesn't? Oh, that's interesting. Now, what happens if you're distracted partway through casting?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T20:41:20-07:00","id":1076266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076264#post1076264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have not; and I know virtually nothing about it. From what I tried reading, it sounded like another attempt at techno-magic (that's what came to mind when I read the term 'technocracy') and I lost interest in it for the same reason I lost interest in God Machine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, in Mage the Ascension, you do have consensual reality. I'm going through this quick, but, a long time ago you had wizards in their towers wreaking havoc and doing what they wanted. And so a bunch of 'good' wizards decided it was wrong. They created a group called the Order of Reason, I just got that name. And they agree upon a paradigm, how the world works, and spread understanding and education about it, to a point, throughout the world. Suddenly these lone mages couldn't do their crazy magic because Joe peasant knew fire needed fuel, and angry tower-dweller's willpower was not fuel. The Order of Reason figured the only way to keep these reality deviants in line and keep them from wrecking up the world and its people was to keep this Reason thing going. Hundreds of years later, as power corrupts, they became the Technocracy. Now they are, for the most part, in control of reality as they have fingers into almost every source of information there is and they control education throughout the world. You can play as a member, they're pretty cool but mostly seen as baddies. Standard gameplay, however, has you be one of the Traditions. These are mages, called reality deviants and hunted by the Technocracy, who refuse to believe in what the world is selling, because they know reality is mutable, that they can make what they want of the world, though they face Paradox when stretching the limits of reality too far. The Traditions have their own belief systems, some thousands of years old, and they use their their magic to force them on the world, ideally to break the Technocracy's hold on it.<br /> <br /> It actually sounds a lot more like what you want than Awakening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrBreaksIt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076265#post1076265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, look, all science is is a way of observing the world. That's it. If something can be observed and repeated then it can be studied scientifically. It can be quantified. If magic cannot be observed and cannot be repeated then there is simply no way it can work.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, without putting words in his mouth, Nyrufa's problem seems to be more about traditional science trappings than science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-10-2017, 11:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T20:48:24-07:00","id":1076268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076266#post1076266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It actually sounds a lot more like what you want than Awakening.<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That actually does sound very close to my view on the subject. Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, I kind of remember reading about how the whole Technocracy decided to suppress the supernatural at one point, which blew up in their face when they decided to put a man on the moon and brought back the fairies!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T20:56:28-07:00","id":1076271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076268#post1076268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That actually does sound very close to my view on the subject. Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, I kind of remember reading about how the whole Technocracy decided to suppress the supernatural at one point, which blew up in their face when they decided to put a man on the moon and brought back the fairies!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, the Technocracy does not like magic or the supernatural, they're good antagonists. I don't know much about Changeling but from what I recall they thrive on hope, and going to the moon brought a lot of that down to Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T21:03:07-07:00","id":1076274,"title":"","content":"One of the theses of the Chronicles of Darkness is that the everyday world is a pretty fucking magical place, and that this shows through as much when you're playing with diesel or fiberoptics as when you're playing with sigils or rings of salt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T21:11:34-07:00","id":1076277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076271#post1076271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, the Technocracy does not like magic or the supernatural, they're good antagonists. I don't know much about Changeling but from what I recall they thrive on hope, and going to the moon brought a lot of that down to Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> As I understand it, the fairies in Dreaming are literally products of human imagination. That's why the Age of Reason started to kill them all off, because humanity's belief in the supernatural was declining. And when the first man landed on the moon, there was a small window in which the whole world believed anything was possible. That window allowed the Fey to come flooding back into the world, and they now struggle to keep the spark of creativity alive in the hearts of mankind.<br /> <br /> They could, in a sense, be the arch rivals to the Technocracy, if you want to go that route.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T21:19:14-07:00","id":1076278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076027#post1076027\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought Mage intentionally left it ambiguous as to whether or not Mage Arcadia and Changeling Arcadia were one in the same. So it was ultimately up to the players to decide how they wanted to treat it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think we'll ever rule on it conclusively in a book -- there's no need to explicitly wall off that point of crossover. But with the Supernal as it's evolved through late first edition and now into second edition, and with what we're doing with Changeling's Arcadia in second edition, they don't really resemble each other. And we wouldn't want to compromise our portrayal of either the Supernal or faerie in order to maintain the potential for a connection that never went much further than the name.<br /> <br /> If you see ways to connect the two, go ahead and do it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: To be clear, while it goes beyond this, the difference includes the Supernal as mages understand it not being a physical place, while Faerie as changelings experience it is a <i>very</i> physical place. You can breathe the air and drink the water and sail the oceans and cut yourself open on the swords, and those things are as plain and literal as if you did them on Earth.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 04-11-2017, 12:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T21:22:21-07:00","id":1076282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076250#post1076250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's how MY version of magic works; which is the point I have been trying to clarify from the start of this discussion.<br /> <br /> <b>In MY version of magic; it can not be quantified or studied because the variables are ever changing. </b>Magic functions in the manner that is presented because the mage using it wants the magic to function in that fashion. It has nothing to do with scientific reasoning or physics. It's concentrated desire forced upon the world. Anybody with a comparably strong willpower or opposing desire could effectively cancel out their magic. Not because of the nature of opposing forces, but simply because they wanted their desired outcome more strongly than their opponent.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quick rant as relates to my tastes and understandings:<br /> <br /> The rest of what you describe is not in accordance to the bolded, nor should it, because it describes magic as a non-repeatable affair, neither a thing you can replicate or anticipate and therefore not a thing you can take advantage of-magic just happens when it will. Now that's cool if magic is a setting thing rather than a character thing, and in fact I'd be down for a game on that premise-but if you're in a game where you can use magic, a character has to at least figure out how it should be able to be invoked in even your most insane of space-time-circumstances confluences- magic might only be a thing you are able to invoke on the 66th half moon of the this current cycle of the world at the crossroads of three empires when surrounded by the blood of ewes <i>this one time</i>, but a character has to be able to figure that out if it's going to mean jack-and/or-shit at all, which supposes a discernable system by which will is manifested into the miraculous action. Discernable phenomenon can be cycled down into the development of understanding and precision knowledge of hows and whys, albeit as it goes on, and thus goes on from just &quot;weird shit happens&quot; to science and technology. If you can take advantage of it, there is a science and technological place for it.<br /> <br /> Let me put it another way-the only game I've seen come close to having their special shit act the way you describe it is, ironically, Genius the Trangression, and that's....not good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T21:46:58-07:00","id":1076289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076282#post1076282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick rant as relates to my tastes and understandings:<br /> <br /> The rest of what you describe is not in accordance to the bolded, nor should it, because it describes magic as a non-repeatable affair, neither a thing you can replicate or anticipate and therefore not a thing you can take advantage of-magic just happens when it will. Now that's cool if magic is a setting thing rather than a character thing, and in fact I'd be down for a game on that premise-but if you're in a game where you can use magic, a character has to at least figure out how it should be able to be invoked in even your most insane of space-time-circumstances confluences- magic might only be a thing you are able to invoke on the 66th half moon of the this current cycle of the world at the crossroads of three empires when surrounded by the blood of ewes <i>this one time</i>, but a character has to be able to figure that out if it's going to mean jack-and/or-shit at all, which supposes a discernable system by which will is manifested into the miraculous action. Discernable phenomenon can be cycled down into the development of understanding and precision knowledge of hows and whys, albeit as it goes on, and thus goes on from just &quot;weird shit happens&quot; to science and technology. If you can take advantage of it, there is a science and technological place for it.<br /> <br /> Let me put it another way-the only game I've seen come close to having their special shit act the way you describe it is, ironically, Genius the Trangression, and that's....not good.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The overall outcome of the magic can be repeated, but the circumstances behind their performance might not always be possible. It is the Mage's willpower that brings the magic to fruition, not the result of a controlled environment. A mage could cast the exact same spell the exact same way three times in a row and then suddenly decide (voluntarily or not) that the spell no longer works that way; thus resulting in complications the next time they try to cast it.<br /> <br /> I already gave a sample run down of my rules for the treatment and use of magic. What you consider scientific observation is nothing more than a placebo effect to my idea of mages. It can stabilize their focus, making it easier to work the desired spell; but it does not have any real effect on the spell's performance.<br /> <br /> THAT is the kind of magic that I know and love. Scientific, quantifiable magic is not appealing to me. Like, at all; I immediately lose interest in it the moment somebody figures out a way to apply science into the mix.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076278#post1076278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I don't think we'll ever rule on it conclusively in a book -- there's no need to explicitly wall off that point of crossover. But with the Supernal as it's evolved through late first edition and now into second edition, and with what we're doing with Changeling's Arcadia in second edition, they don't really resemble each other. And we wouldn't want to compromise our portrayal of either the Supernal or faerie in order to maintain the potential for a connection that never went much further than the name.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">If you see ways to connect the two, go ahead and do it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">EDIT: To be clear, while it goes beyond this, the difference includes the Supernal as mages understand it not being a physical place, while Faerie as changelings experience it is a <i>very</i> physical place. You can breathe the air and drink the water and sail the oceans and cut yourself open on the swords, and those things are as plain and literal as if you did them on Earth.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I'm actually curious to see how Acanthus mages and Fae Touched mortals will interact with each other. From what we've been told, it sounds like they both take a trip through Arcadia and return with supernatural abilities. It's just that Mages come away with significantly more power.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-11-2017, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T21:58:01-07:00","id":1076297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076289#post1076289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The overall outcome of the magic can be repeated, but the circumstances behind their performance might not always be possible. It is the Mage's willpower that brings the magic to fruition, not the result of a controlled environment. A mage could cast the exact same spell the exact same way three times in a row and then suddenly decide (voluntarily or not) that the spell no longer works that way; thus resulting in complications the next time they try to cast it.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>*looks at you*<br /> <br /> *looks at Yantras, Praxes and Rotes, the mere fact that one can plan out their spells in response to their environments at all, and more*<br /> <br /> *look back at you*<br /> <br /> Sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T22:05:19-07:00","id":1076302,"title":"","content":"I think a more accurate version of what you're trying to say is that magic has no ties to the laws of nature as far we have proven or strongly rely on our current understanding of rather than saying magic that is unscientific or not technology, since the latter two are technically impossible but the former is totally viable in the world of colliding metaphysics that is the Chronicles world. EDIT: Or, in fact, in any other setting that has magic in it.<br /> <br /> Which is also very distinct from a non-repeatable, nigh-on/unanticpatory set of causes-and-effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-11-2017, 01:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T22:07:00-07:00","id":1076303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076297#post1076297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*looks at you*<br /> <br /> *looks at Yantras, Praxes and Rotes, the mere fact that one can plan out their spells in response to their environments at all, and more*<br /> <br /> *look back at you*<br /> <br /> Sure.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay, once again (since I already pointed this out twice), I am talking about <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u><i><b>my personal</b></i></u></span> treatment of magic. Not White Wolf's, not Lovecraft's, not D&amp;D's, not any other popular fiction or media. The rules of magic that I stated are how I personally treat the use of magic. If you have a different idea for how it would / should work, that is perfectly fine for whatever universal setting you wish to implement it.<br /> <br /> <i>But it will not be present in a setting of my creation.</i><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T22:07:43-07:00","id":1076306,"title":"","content":"If willpower is the mechanism by which magic works - if a person can demonstrate the ability to make fire or whatever because they will it - that is an observable phenomenon, and science will seek to incorporate that into its understanding. If you can prove that you can make something happen just because you want it to, then science must accept that and incorporate it into its model of the universe or it is not doing its job.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T22:13:28-07:00","id":1076307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076303#post1076303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Okay, once again (since I already pointed this out twice), I am talking about <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u><i><b>my personal</b></i></u></span> treatment of magic. Not White Wolf's, not Lovecraft's, not D&amp;D's, not any other popular fiction or media. The rules of magic that I stated are how I personally treat the use of magic. If you have a different idea for how it would / should work, that is perfectly fine for whatever universal setting you wish to implement it.<br /> <br /> <i>But it will not be present in a setting of my creation.</i><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough, so long as we remember that I started off my set of comments with establishing what is my personal tastes and peeves in kind. The street can go both ways.<br /> <br /> Although there is still the matter of vocab usage, but whatever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T22:14:27-07:00","id":1076308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076303#post1076303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, once again (since I already pointed this out twice), I am talking about <span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u><i><b>my personal</b></i></u></span> treatment of magic. Not White Wolf's, not Lovecraft's, not D&amp;D's, not any other popular fiction or media. The rules of magic that I stated are how I personally treat the use of magic. If you have a different idea for how it would / should work, that is perfectly fine for whatever universal setting you wish to implement it.<br /> <br /> <i>But it will not be present in a setting of my creation.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>The way you are describing your personal view of Magic working, while it absolutely shatters all natural laws by modern understanding, still does follow its own internally consistent rules (the Mage wills it and it is so - cause and effect). Which means a thorough analysis could form a working model of those rules. Which is the scientific process in action. The processes you are describing as how you think Magic should work are sufficiently advanced technology, whether you like thinking about them that way or not. Because again, science is nothing more and nothing less than a process of analyzing and explaining what you observe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-11-2017, 01:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T22:16:02-07:00","id":1076309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076306#post1076306\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If willpower is the mechanism by which magic works - if a person can demonstrate the ability to make fire or whatever because they will it - that is an observable phenomenon, and science will seek to incorporate that into its understanding. If you can prove that you can make something happen just because you want it to, then science must accept that and incorporate it into its model of the universe or it is not doing its job.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Just because science accepts it does not mean it is capable of explaining it. Why does subject A)'s willpower have the ability to produce spontaneous flame when subject B) does not. And why does proximity to subject C) cause a disruption in subject A)'s performance 30% of the time?<br /> <br /> The answer is all three subjects in unison declaring &quot;I think, therefor I am!&quot;<br /> <br /> You talk about how science is the process by which we observe and explain the world around us. But how do you apply science to somebody who can change the rules any time they want? Simple answer is that you can't. By the time you figured out how they did it; they've switched things up and now you have to start all over again!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-11-2017, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T22:26:12-07:00","id":1076310,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076309#post1076309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because science accepts it does not mean it is capable of explaining it. Why does subject A)'s willpower have the ability to produce spontaneous flame when subject B) does not. And why does proximity to subject C) cause a disruption in subject A)'s performance 30% of the time?<br /> <br /> The answer is all three subjects in unison declaring <b>&quot;I think, therefor I am!&quot;</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Science can't explain why mass causes Spacetime to warp, only that it does so. Science can't explain why objects in motion stay in motion unless acted upon by an opposing Force and objects at rest unless acted upon by an opposing force, only that they do so. Science can't explain why some particles behave like waves under certain circumstances but not when directly observed, only that they do so. Science seeks to break complex processes down to their most fundamental components, but those fundamental components cannot be explained, only described, and those descriptions can be used to explain more complex processes. Scientifically speaking, &quot;I think, therefore I am&quot; is simply the most fundamental component of the complex process you are choosing to call Magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T22:29:50-07:00","id":1076311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076309#post1076309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how do you apply science to somebody who can change the rules any time they want? Simple answer is that you can't. By the time you figured out how they did it; they've switched things up and now you have to start all over again!</div> </div> </div> </div>The <i>simple answer</i> is that if that somebody is <i>a somebody </i>and not <i>a meaningless contrarian hole in space</i> then their tastes will make themselves known in a fashion that can be gleaned through direct or indirect observation.<br /> <br /> Shockingly, people are people regardless of whether or not they have magic powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T22:33:39-07:00","id":1076315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076310#post1076310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Science can't explain why mass causes Spacetime to warp, only that it does so. Science can't explain why objects in motion stay in motion unless acted upon by an opposing Force and objects at rest unless acted upon by an opposing force, only that they do so. Science can't explain why some particles behave like waves under certain circumstances but not when directly observed, only that they do so. Science seeks to break complex processes down to their most fundamental components, but those fundamental components cannot be explained, only described, and those descriptions can be used to explain more complex processes. Scientifically speaking, &quot;I think, therefore I am&quot; is simply the most fundamental component of the complex process you are choosing to call Magic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Seems pretty straight forward on the object in motion bit. It's being carried by the momentum / kinetic energy that caused it to start moving in the first place. And the opposing object or force siphons off that energy, causing it to come to a stop once more. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T22:59:40-07:00","id":1076320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076309#post1076309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You talk about how science is the process by which we observe and explain the world around us. But how do you apply science to somebody who can change the rules any time they want? Simple answer is that you can't. By the time you figured out how they did it; they've switched things up and now you have to start all over again!</div> </div> </div> </div>That just means you need a better hypothesis! We always reach a point where our limited tools of observation prevent us from learning more, but then we invent better tools and keep on trucking. It's theoretically possible that we might reach a point where we cannot develop any better tools, but that's not happening anytime soon.<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Any sufficiently analyzed magic becomes technology.&quot;</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/484-iry","name":"Iry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar484_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"346"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-10T23:30:53-07:00","id":1076330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076315#post1076315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Seems pretty straight forward on the object in motion bit. It's being carried by the momentum / kinetic energy that caused it to start moving in the first place. And the opposing object or force siphons off that energy, causing it to come to a stop once more.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, so <b>why </b>does energy cause something to move? Science can't explain that. All it can explain is that things move when energy is applied to it. It never can prove why, nor it has to, nor it needs to.<br /> <br /> You say how someone who changes the rules is outside science. That seems true... but how is that someone changing the rules? Does he have something called, say, a preference? As in, guidelines to how he will change things under what circumstances? Well, that's a rule, and science can observe that. Social sciences are a thing.<br /> <br /> Or does that reality warper do things completely random, without no guidelines behind his will? Okay, now that's an interesting phenomena. But the changes that reality warper brings are real, right? As in, the changes have a defined effect on the world? Then we can observe the fallout and consequences of the changes the reality warper brings. That's knowledge, acquired via science. Then we, although we'll have do jack trying to manipulate the reality warper, at least be able to prepare ourselves for the next reality warping. That's technology, acquired through practical applications of knowledge, gathered by science.<br /> <br /> <br /> And speaking of Mage The Ascension... If the only issue you have is that you want magic to be purely will-working, then it'll fit for you. But you also seem to have this schema that defines magic as everything non-technological. Sorry to tell you this, but even in MtAs, magic is technological. No, I'm not talking about the Technocracy and other technomancers, although they're the most explicit. Even the non-technomantic Traditions and Crafts use technology. Why? Because they study <i>how </i>they can change Consensual Reality with their beliefs and wills, compile the observed results, apply it to other stuff to see if what their wills and beliefs really work, and pass on that accumulated knowledge to others. It's why they have Practices and Foci, Paradigms, Rotes, and Grimoires. It's how they came up with the Nine Spheres. All of that is technology. It's just that the Mystic faction uses technology on things we modern humans don't usually think to apply technology on, such as angels and spirits and inner demons of the mind and extra-sensory perception and so on.<br /> <br /> Oh, but you also define technology as its most limited and narrow form: stuff we modern people use in our lives. So yeah, maybe you might perceive Mystics as not using technology and therefore &quot;true&quot; magic, when their traditions (and Traditions) <i>thrive </i>on it.<br /> <br /> As a side note, archamges in MtAs can seemingly manipulate reality with only Will, using none of the Practices and Foci and all such technological stuff. However, even they work with Paradigms so deeply internalized that they're able to skip the menial parts. And what is a Paradigm, but a carefully constructed theory of the world? Construction which requires observation, hypotheses, and confirmation, all of which is science?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T00:50:53-07:00","id":1076357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076315#post1076315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems pretty straight forward on the object in motion bit. It's being carried by the momentum / kinetic energy that caused it to start moving in the first place. And the opposing object or force siphons off that energy, causing it to come to a stop once more. </div> </div> </div> </div>That's not an explanation it's a tautology. Energy is simply the ability to do work. What you're basically saying is that objects in motion stay in motion because they are carried by their movement. Yes, that's what motion is, but you have done nothing to further anyone's understanding of why that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T04:40:02-07:00","id":1076410,"title":"","content":"Hmm, well I'd say that the paradigms and rules of each sphere / arcana make sense from a logical standpoint. If you want to create a glass of water, ignite a campfire, or spy on somebody 20 miles away, then chances are you probably aren't going to use Death magic (unless you're scanning for the scene of a murder?). Death magic encapsulates magic that pertains to the forces of death. If you try to do something that does not involve death, then you aren't using Death magic, you're using something else.<br /> <br /> But to a true reality warper, these rules and spheres of influence would be illusions constructed by limited minds. They're labels and guidelines that somebody decided to slap onto their abilities in order to explain them easier. A true reality warper who has unlocked their full potential has no need for such preconceptions.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Magic is magic. Just as water is water. It matters only in how it is used.&quot;</i> - Solas, Dragon Age: Inquisition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T04:59:04-07:00","id":1076415,"title":"","content":"What does that have to do with anything at all?<br /> Look, you seem to be under the impression that we believe the underlying processes by which will becomes magic can be explained and turned into machines, but we're not. We're observing that will turning into magic is the process and that observation is science. As long as we can clearly see that this person can light things on fire because they want to light things on fire without going through the intervening steps it is still bloody scientific!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4968-mrbreaksit","name":"MrBreaksIt","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"130"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T05:01:49-07:00","id":1076417,"title":"","content":"Quick question for Nyrufa: If a sorcerer tries to practice his Fireball spell to figure out how he can make it stronger, is it science?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T05:02:53-07:00","id":1076418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076244#post1076244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> But how do you quantify Will and Symbology? I'm pretty sure that the scientific community doesn't accept the claim<b> &amp;quot;this works because I believe that it works&amp;quot;</b> when attempting to explain something. Science demands evidence and proof, not outstanding claims and baseless speculation. That very mage (or even another one, entirely) could turn around and say <b>&amp;quot;now I believe that it doesn't work!&amp;quot;</b> It is for that reason that Will Working and Hard Science can not mutually exist. By their very definitions, they cancel each other out.</div> </div> </div> </div>In mage you quantify it with mage sight, with Unveiling and Knowing Practices. It's magic because it's a hidden process, which technique might involve tools or the expenditure (ie the burning) of Mana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T05:32:27-07:00","id":1076422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076417#post1076417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quick question for Nyrufa: If a sorcerer tries to practice his Fireball spell to figure out how he can make it stronger, is it science?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Don't think there's a satisfactory answer for that. I seem to have a fundamentally different understanding of what science is compared to everybody else here. For me, all the sorcerer needs to improve their Fireball is believe that it's better; assuming that there isn't anyone around with a stronger belief that conflicts with the spell they're trying to cast. No further explanation need be given on the subject. The sorcerer doesn't need to know how it works, all that matters is that it does.<br /> <br /> But it sounds like for you, the sorcerer would spend arduous hours casting the spell over and over again with different intervals in casting times as they compiled research notes (physical and mental) on how the spell works. Can they accelerate its travel speed for greater moment, or reduce it for better precision? Can they throttle the flames, or absorb heat from the surrounding environment? All good possibilities that could be studied and applied to making a stronger fireball. But it doesn't carry the fundamental essence of what reality warping is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T05:50:10-07:00","id":1076426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076422#post1076422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Don't think there's a satisfactory answer for that. I seem to have a fundamentally different understanding of what science is compared to everybody else here. For me, all the sorcerer needs to improve their Fireball is believe that it's better; assuming that there isn't anyone around with a stronger belief that conflicts with the spell they're trying to cast. No further explanation need be given on the subject. The sorcerer doesn't need to know how it works, all that matters is that it does.<br /> <br /> But it sounds like for you, the sorcerer would spend arduous hours casting the spell over and over again with different intervals in casting times as they compiled research notes (physical and mental) on how the spell works. Can they accelerate its travel speed for greater moment, or reduce it for better precision? Can they throttle the flames, or absorb heat from the surrounding environment? All good possibilities that could be studied and applied to making a stronger fireball. But it doesn't carry the fundamental essence of what reality warping is.</div> </div> </div> </div>How much opposing will is necessary to stop their will? Would thinking differently help? Others reinforcing your will instead of opposing it?<br /> <br /> The practiced discovery of all/any of these factors is science.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T05:58:47-07:00","id":1076428,"title":"","content":"Let's put this a slightly different way... ever heard someone describe something as &quot;a science&quot;? Like, &quot;cooking is a science&quot; for example?* They don't say that because it involves machinery (though of course it <i>can</i> and often does). The reason is that there's a <i>repeatable process</i> to it. If there's a method that an individual with the proper tools and skills (say, the gift of magic and a grasp of its use) can follow to produce consistent results, and can then explain to others with the same skills and tools how they achieved the end result, then that's a science. Doesn't matter if that method is as simple as &quot;briefly focusing their conscious will and belief toward a desired end, any other flourishes are fun but optional&quot; or as complex as &quot;while wearing a crown of iron and a chain consisting of 49 links of electrum, swirling a nine-inch birch wand through the air clockwise three times, reciting a haiku composed in proto-Latin, and flooding their own mind with thoughts of righteous anger&quot;.<br /> <br /> Now, if they're not using a method (even one as simple as consciously deciding something should happen), and if no outside factors can influence the events in any way - if stuff is just <i>happening</i> around them with absolutely no pattern of initiation or repetition, nor any rhyme or reason to <i>what</i> is happening - then sure, that's probably not really classifiable as a &quot;science&quot; of any sort. But then, they're not really in control of it either, so it's not really &quot;their&quot; magic for most purposes.<br /> <br /> In short, any sorcerer worth their 343 grams of refined salt extracted from the dead sea on the night of a full moon is going to find themselves referring to magic as &quot;a science&quot;, though perhaps with different superficial trappings, and an ascendant reality warper with time to muse on the subject stands at least a chance of agreeing.**<br /> <br /> * Yes, I know people will say &quot;cooking is an art&quot; too, but bear with me here.<br /> ** Before they turn said sorcerer into a jackalope, because everyone needs a pet.***<br /> *** Incidentally, the reality warper has decreed that the human mindset <i>demands</i> the acquisition and care of one or more pets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I've got a bit of a bad habit of extensively editing my posts after the fact. Please try and bear with me...<br /> In case you're comfortable being more friendly and casual about things, my name's Seren, or Es/Es for short. They/Them or Fae/Faer, please.","edited":{"userid":3946,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","user":"Sconce","date":". 04-11-2017, 09:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3946-sconce","name":"Sconce","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T06:00:02-07:00","id":1076429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076422#post1076422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I seem to have a fundamentally different understanding of what science is compared to everybody else here.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does seem to be the issue, yes. Vent0 made my point before me, you don't need a notepad to do science. &quot;If I gain more confidence in my ability to shoot a Fireball, then I'll be able to shoot better Fireballs&quot; *is* science.<br /> <br /> If you allow me a follow-up question: Is language technology?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T06:15:53-07:00","id":1076436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076429#post1076429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you allow me a follow-up question: Is language technology?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, good one. In this context it reminds me of those theories where written language is both a form a technology and a way to assert a magical paradigm that nowadays is almost omnipresent.<br /> <br /> Ascension and The Invisibles. Good times.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T06:56:40-07:00","id":1076453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076429#post1076429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If you allow me a follow-up question: Is language technology?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not... really? No. It's a series of audio / visual signals that we have been trained to interpret various meanings from. The same way a caveman learns not to stick their hand in fire because they receive pain signals telling him &quot;THIS IS BAD AND YOU SHOULD FEEL BAD!&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> The reason why I'm having a hard time accepting your variation of what science is, is largely due to my exposure with religious debate throughout the course of my life. Namely how people demanding a scientific explanation for things refuse to accept <b>&quot;God did it&quot;</b> as a proper explanation. And when they ask how God did it, they refuse to accept <b>&quot;they're God, they can do anything!&quot;</b> as a suitable reason. Real world science refuses to acknowledge my ideas of magic and the supernatural. So I naturally learned to view magic and science as two different things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-11-2017, 10:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T07:16:45-07:00","id":1076465,"title":"","content":"*Facepalms* Language is tech. It's derided off a concensus, it follows rules made out of convenience and we're constantly adapting it. Tell me how that's different from say, a software.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T07:21:44-07:00","id":1076468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076453#post1076453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not... really? No. <b>It's a series of audio / visual signals that we have been trained to interpret various meanings from</b>. The same way a caveman learns not to stick their hand in fire because they receive pain signals telling him &quot;THIS IS BAD AND YOU SHOULD FEEL BAD!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. Plenty of people on this thread could argue that yes, it is a form of technology, much more eloquently that I'll ever be able to.<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The reason why I'm having a hard time accepting your variation of what science is, is largely due to my exposure with religious debate throughout the course of my life. Namely how people demanding a scientific explanation for things refuse to accept &quot;God did it&quot; as a proper explanation for things.So I naturally learned to view magic and science as two different things. </div> </div> </div>Understandable, then.<br /> I'm going to go back to a point made earlier in this thread, that science doesn't explain <i>why</i> gravity works, it only tells us <i>how</i> it works. That distinction right there is important. That distinction means that, using science, you can't prove (or disprove, for that matter) the existence of the Divine. For all science cares about, gravity works the way it does <i>because God willed it so</i>.<br /> My point is, even if &quot;Magic&quot; can fill in the <i>why</i> part, science will always be able to fill in the <i>how</i> part, as they aren't at all exclusive.<br /> Sidebar:<div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">Anyone telling you that scientists don't/can't believe in God is flat-out wrong. Roger Bacon, who is often credited with formalizing the scientific method, was a Franciscan friar. Georges Lema\u00eetre, a Belgian Catholic Priest, astronomer and professor of physics at the Catholic University of Leuven, proposed what became known as the Big Bang theory.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T07:45:40-07:00","id":1076487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076453#post1076453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason why I'm having a hard time accepting your variation of what science is, is largely due to my exposure with religious debate throughout the course of my life. Namely how people demanding a scientific explanation for things refuse to accept <b>&quot;God did it&quot;</b> as a proper explanation. And when they ask how God did it, they refuse to accept <b>&quot;they're God, they can do anything!&quot;</b> as a suitable reason. Real world science refuses to acknowledge my ideas of magic and the supernatural. So I naturally learned to view magic and science as two different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason science refuses to accept &quot;God did it&quot; is because there is no empirical evidence to support this claim. Science is a process of explaining what can be observed, and God cannot be observed (by definition in the case of the God of Christianity). If empirical evidence of God could be given, and this evidence could be verified by multiple researchers under controlled conditions, science would have to accept God as a thing that exists and do its best to explain God's existence.<br /> <br /> The thing is, the existence of a supreme being or beings is something that must be taken on faith. This magic you are talking about is not. It can be performed, observed, and repeated in controlled environments, so it can be empirically proven to exist, which means science must accept its existence and work to understand and explain it. Even if that means throwing out everything we thought we knew about thermodynamics because if fire can be created and sustained by nothing but will, then apparently the laws we thought were universally true regarding heat energy must not apply in all circumstances. A good scientist would be <i>thrilled</i> by such a discovery, and be eager to figure out how this willpower-fuelled fire works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-11-2017, 10:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T08:06:58-07:00","id":1076497,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076231#post1076231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. If something can provably be done in violation of the laws of physics (like, for example, creating fire with no catalyst that burns with no fuel), a good scientist doesnt state dumbfounded and protest &quot;but that's against the <i>rules</i>!&quot; A good scientist asks &quot;how was my understanding of the laws of physics wrong?&quot; If fuelless fire can be made by repeatable processes, it doesn't matter if those processes fit within the current understanding of science, science will adapt to account for this new possibility. Because science isn't a system of rules, it's a process of explaining how things work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> YES So much YES !!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T08:36:21-07:00","id":1076513,"title":"","content":"Fantasy is just sci fi with alternate laws of physics.<br /> <br /> The Wyrd, the Supernal, the Divine Fire, all of it has rules that govern it functions, just like gravity, electric magnatizism, heat, and so on. No Supernatural being just thinks whatever it wants and makes it happen without utiliizing some force with a set of laws as to it functioning. <br /> <br /> The Gentry and other Fae use the Wyrd which is a force or phenomena in the CoD.<br /> <br /> Prommies use the Divine Fire and Alchemy with its own set of rules like chemistry, but its a different set of rules then chemistry.<br /> <br /> Sin Eaters, Ghosts, and Chthrothlathions obey the physics of the alternste dimesion the Underworld including those that govern its interactions with earth.<br /> <br /> Spirits and Werewolves do the same with the Hisil.<br /> <br /> The Supernal World appears to just be the code of reality, its own law of physics. I suggest reading The Holographic Universe before looking at 2e Mage Cosmology.<br /> <br /> Deviants are often the product of scientific experimentation.<br /> <br /> Mummies are influenced by the physics of another altetnate dimesion.<br /> <br /> Vampires too if they were created by the Strix, they follow the laws of physics dictating the interaction between the Dark Place and the Earth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T08:39:17-07:00","id":1076516,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076487#post1076487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reason science refuses to accept &amp;quot;God did it&amp;quot; is because there is no empirical evidence to support this claim. Science is a process of explaining what can be observed, and God cannot be observed (by definition in the case of the God of Christianity). If empirical evidence of God could be given, and this evidence could be verified by multiple researchers under controlled conditions, science would have to accept God as a thing that exists and do its best to explain God's existence.<br /> <br /> The thing is, the existence of a supreme being or beings is something that must be taken on faith. This magic you are talking about is not. It can be performed, observed, and repeated in controlled environments, so it can be empirically proven to exist, which means science must accept its existence and work to understand and explain it. Even if that means throwing out everything we thought we knew about thermodynamics because if fire can be created and sustained by nothing but will, then apparently the laws we thought were universally true regarding heat energy must not apply in all circumstances. A good scientist would be <i>thrilled</i> by such a discovery, and be eager to figure out how this willpower-fuelled fire works.</div> </div> </div> </div> That means just about all the &quot;magic&quot; in CoD really is a type of alternate physical laws.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T09:02:29-07:00","id":1076526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076487#post1076487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The reason science refuses to accept &quot;God did it&quot; is because there is no empirical evidence to support this claim. Science is a process of explaining what can be observed, and God cannot be observed (by definition in the case of the God of Christianity). If empirical evidence of God could be given, and this evidence could be verified by multiple researchers under controlled conditions, science would have to accept God as a thing that exists and do its best to explain God's existence.<br /> <br /> The thing is, the existence of a supreme being or beings is something that must be taken on faith. This magic you are talking about is not. It can be performed, observed, and repeated in controlled environments, so it can be empirically proven to exist, which means science must accept its existence and work to understand and explain it. Even if that means throwing out everything we thought we knew about thermodynamics because if fire can be created and sustained by nothing but will, then apparently the laws we thought were universally true regarding heat energy must not apply in all circumstances. A good scientist would be <i>thrilled</i> by such a discovery, and be eager to figure out how this willpower-fuelled fire works.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Makes sense, I suppose.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T09:25:31-07:00","id":1076540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076516#post1076516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> That means just about all the &amp;quot;magic&amp;quot; in CoD really is a type of alternate physical laws.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point exactly. And, I suspect, Clarke's point in his Third Law. All &quot;magic&quot; is just not-yet-fully-understood science.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://youtu.be/E8vx-OtYYZY\" data-code=\"E8vx-OtYYZY\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/E8vx-OtYYZY/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T09:57:56-07:00","id":1076555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076297#post1076297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*looks at you*<br /> <br /> *looks at Yantras, Praxes and Rotes, the mere fact that one can plan out their spells in response to their environments at all, and more*<br /> <br /> *look back at you*<br /> <br /> Sure.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Arc, you need to stop making posts like this. You've been given a lot of leeway in the past for bullying other posters like this, but that can't keep going on. This is the last warning I'm going to give you, if this pattern continues your posting privileges will be suspended.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T11:59:53-07:00","id":1076609,"title":"","content":"I would argue that the split is not between Magic and science, but between Magic and technology.<br /> \u200bScience is just applying the scientific method to an observed phenomenon, something most modern people do out of conditioned reflex.<br /> Technology is the tools created from what is learned, science's practical application as it were.<br /> The difference is anyone can use the technology, even though they have no clue how it works.<br /> <br /> Magic requires knowledge and insight, the ignorant can't do it.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T12:00:41-07:00","id":1076610,"title":"","content":"I don't think we're talking about the God-Machine anymore, most of this has shifted to something that should really be on The Mage Forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13063-lord-jub-jub","name":"Lord Jub-Jub","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13063_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T12:08:47-07:00","id":1076617,"title":"","content":"The way I view God-Machine fluff is that the scientific method can never be used to fully understand the GM, there are too many missing variables, too much an observer can't detect or quantify.<br /> \u200bThat is what makes it 'high weirdness', in spite of its quasi scientific appearance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T13:30:19-07:00","id":1076644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076610#post1076610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we're talking about the God-Machine anymore, most of this has shifted to something that should really be on The Mage Forum.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I'd say it belongs here in the general CoD section rather than Mage. The discussion seems to mostly be about the difference/definition of science compared to that of magic. And when I say magic I'm not talking Awakened magic, but magic in general, including the god machine/demons brand of science themed magic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076617#post1076617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The way I view God-Machine fluff is that the scientific method can never be used to fully understand the GM, there are too many missing variables, too much an observer can't detect or quantify.<br /> \u200bThat is what makes it 'high weirdness', in spite of its quasi scientific appearance.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the scientific method <i>could</i> be used to fully understand the GM, but it is so vast and complex that it would take such a crazy amount of time to do so as to functionally be impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2309,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","user":"Ashenrogue","date":". 04-11-2017, 04:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T13:58:26-07:00","id":1076656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Jub-Jub</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076610#post1076610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think we're talking about the God-Machine anymore, most of this has shifted to something that should really be on The Mage Forum.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mage, Changeling, really any of the splats capable of using high end occult powers. But as I already said, my trouble with identifying the scientific aspect of magic came from real world upbringing, which Charlaquin did a decent job of putting a more appropriate explanation on than the one I had come to know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T21:42:15-07:00","id":1076800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076609#post1076609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Magic requires knowledge and insight, the ignorant can't do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is a specific conceit to gaming to make magic-users special (so your fighter can't just have a stash of fireball spells and be able to match the wizard that knows them), because this is extremely common in fiction. &quot;A person reads a spell aloud from a book without knowing what it will do, bad stuff ensues,&quot; it the basic premise of a bunch of fantasy/horror stories.<br /> <br /> Even the CofD incorporates this as normal humans can accidentally activate plot-device oriented magical items or things like Infrastructure. Such events are never on par with the various magic users of the playable kind, but the idea is still part of the games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T21:47:40-07:00","id":1076802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076800#post1076800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think this is a specific conceit to gaming to make magic-users special (so your fighter can't just have a stash of fireball spells and be able to match the wizard that knows them), because this is extremely common in fiction. &quot;A person reads a spell aloud from a book without knowing what it will do, bad stuff ensues,&quot; it the basic premise of a bunch of fantasy/horror stories.<br /> <br /> Even the CofD incorporates this as normal humans can accidentally activate plot-device oriented magical items or things like Infrastructure. Such events are never on par with the various magic users of the playable kind, but the idea is still part of the games.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Come to think of it, an adequately 'buffed' wizard could be just as effective in martial combat as a fighter, even if this state only lasts for a short while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-11T21:58:27-07:00","id":1076807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076800#post1076800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think this is a specific conceit to gaming to make magic-users special (so your fighter can't just have a stash of fireball spells and be able to match the wizard that knows them), because this is extremely common in fiction. &quot;A person reads a spell aloud from a book without knowing what it will do, bad stuff ensues,&quot; it the basic premise of a bunch of fantasy/horror stories.</div> </div> </div> </div>ChroD magic that isn't bound to a concretely supernatural locus tends to be exceedingly dependent upon variables like time, place, genealogy, and emotional state, and in a setting where multiple variants of &quot;fate&quot; are metaphorically running around nudging assorted actors into the right configurations it's kind of out of sorts to describe that premise as &quot;the ignorant doing magic&quot; rather than &quot;the ignorant being the catalyst for a magical accident.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T00:51:43-07:00","id":1076845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076802#post1076802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, an adequately 'buffed' wizard could be just as effective in martial combat as a fighter, even if this state only lasts for a short while.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, yes, that's the D&amp;D &quot;Linear Fighter/Quadratic Wizard&quot; issue in a nutshell. Despite attempts to make magic-users weaker in terms of things like being more frail/less skilled in armed combat, the sheer potency of magic use that's limited only to special magic users will outgrow anything else over time/advancement. Both the WoD and CofD have consistently had this, though in most cases less noticeably because it's strongest in crossover games rather than straight games where everyone is playing the same type of creature. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076807#post1076807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">ChroD magic that isn't bound to a concretely supernatural locus tends to be exceedingly dependent upon variables like time, place, genealogy, and emotional state, and in a setting where multiple variants of &quot;fate&quot; are metaphorically running around nudging assorted actors into the right configurations it's kind of out of sorts to describe that premise as &quot;the ignorant doing magic&quot; rather than &quot;the ignorant being the catalyst for a magical accident.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I would chalk this up to the CofD focused on the horror aspect of this. It's designed for things like the Evil Dead movies, not &quot;Xander, don't read Latin in front of the books&quot; from Buffy. The &quot;catalyst for magical accident&quot; sub-type of the &quot;ignorant doing magic,&quot; larger trope is the most compelling for a horror focused game. Though things like Mystery Cults and HtV definitely allow for both as low rank members might do things they don't realize is actually magic while being catalysts for something bigger.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T01:21:05-07:00","id":1076851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076609#post1076609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The difference is anyone can use the technology, even though they have no clue how it works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found this bit hilarious, since I work tech support for a web development company.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T05:03:09-07:00","id":1076908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076278#post1076278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think we'll ever rule on it conclusively in a book -- there's no need to explicitly wall off that point of crossover. But with the Supernal as it's evolved through late first edition and now into second edition, and with what we're doing with Changeling's Arcadia in second edition, they don't really resemble each other. And we wouldn't want to compromise our portrayal of either the Supernal or faerie in order to maintain the potential for a connection that never went much further than the name.<br /> <br /> If you see ways to connect the two, go ahead and do it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: To be clear, while it goes beyond this, the difference includes the Supernal as mages understand it not being a physical place, while Faerie as changelings experience it is a <i>very</i> physical place. You can breathe the air and drink the water and sail the oceans and cut yourself open on the swords, and those things are as plain and literal as if you did them on Earth.</div> </div> </div> </div> I could see Farie being an emination realm of Mage Arcadia if one wanted a connection between the two for crossovers, that would still give Farie physical place to it; without changing the nature of Mage Arcadia","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T05:15:16-07:00","id":1076913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076845#post1076845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, yes, that's the D&amp;D &quot;Linear Fighter/Quadratic Wizard&quot; issue in a nutshell. Despite attempts to make magic-users weaker in terms of things like being more frail/less skilled in armed combat, the sheer potency of magic use that's limited only to special magic users will outgrow anything else over time/advancement. Both the WoD and CofD have consistently had this, though in most cases less noticeably because it's strongest in crossover games rather than straight games where everyone is playing the same type of creature.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>In past editions of D&amp;D, mages had the ability to destroy entire cities at higher levels. I seem to recall a 9th level spell from the oriental setting that just <i>launches a tsunami</i> at people. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the whole frailty weakness, a mage could just use Polymorph, Shapechange, or Tenser's Transformation to turn into a less frail creature. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-12-2017, 08:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T07:28:07-07:00","id":1076957,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076913#post1076913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In past editions of D&amp;D, mages had the ability to destroy entire cities at higher levels. I seem to recall a 9th level spell from the oriental setting that just <i>launches a tsunami</i> at people. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for the whole frailty weakness, a mage could just use Polymorph, Shapechange, or Tenser's Transformation to turn into a less frail creature. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Which, honestly, isn't anything to be happy about.<br /> That's why DnD wizards are badly designed (because they have too much narrative power compared to other people at their level) or alternatively, why DND fighters are badly designed (because they have not enough narrative power compared to other people at their level). If one class gets to cause a tsunami by doing a funny dance and saying few words, another should probably be able to cause a tsunami by stomping really hard.<br /> <br /> Anyway, funny observation:<br /> &quot;I believe really hard so it happens&quot; never really spoke to me as a form of magic. Never liked it. My first instinct when I think of magic - and what I search for when trying to &quot;play&quot; magic - is a set of rules, sympathies and principles that can be observed, understood and exploited. You could say that to make magic feel magical for me, it must follow internal logic that might as visible or as shrouded as the context demands. <br /> Which, in light of this conversation, would mean that...<br /> I want magic to be a technology. <br /> That's funny.<br /> <br /> But it also explains why in many, many settings, mages and magical-equivalents are their society's &quot;analogy&quot; to scientists and researchers, and why what a lot of people called &quot;Mages&quot; was simply early users of poorly-understood &quot;technologies&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-12-2017, 10:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T09:14:47-07:00","id":1077011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076957#post1076957\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, funny observation:<br /> &quot;I believe really hard so it happens&quot; never really spoke to me as a form of magic. Never liked it. My first instinct when I think of magic - and what I search for when trying to &quot;play&quot; magic - is a set of rules, sympathies and principles that can be observed, understood and exploited. You could say that to make magic feel magical for me, it must follow internal logic that might as visible or as shrouded as the context demands.<br /> Which, in light of this conversation, would mean that...<br /> I want magic to be a technology.<br /> That's funny.<br /> <br /> But it also explains why in many, many settings, mages and magical-equivalents are their society's &quot;analogy&quot; to scientists and researchers, and why what a lot of people called &quot;Mages&quot; was simply early users of poorly-understood &quot;technologies&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The whole believing really hard thing is derived from the very idea of Will Working. You are rejecting the established reality and substituting your own in its place; at least in the form I've come to understand.<br /> <br /> <br /> In D&amp;D, the creatures of the Far Realm (basically Lovecraft's works) are beyond our understanding because their universe formed differently than our own. Everything from the laws of physics to the atomic structure of the world is completely different from the rest of the planes. Which is why people who are exposed to that environment often come back as insane mutants. Their minds and bodies couldn't handle a universe that operates on a completely alien structure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=aw-2KuHIYyo\" data-code=\"aw-2KuHIYyo\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/aw-2KuHIYyo/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 04-12-2017, 12:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T09:32:57-07:00","id":1077023,"title":"","content":"Yeah, Nyrufa, I'm pretty sure you would enjoy Mage the Asenscion more than Mage the Awakening. As I understand it, Mage the Asenscion's Magic works based on consensual reality. The more people believe a thing, and the harder they believe it, the more it becomes true. There are certain trends in magical practices (called paradigms) not because those practices are magically potent <i>per se</i>, but because getting a lot of mages believing in the same magical paradigm <i>makes it</i> magically potent. Muggle witnesses can fuck up magical effects that are obviously impossible in their worldview because their collective disbelief in it can cause it to not be possible. And the technocracy that you felt would turn you off of the game is an antagonist group. Mages who use a technology-based magical paradigm and promote advancement of and access to technology among non-magic folk so as to strengthen their own paradigm and weaken others.<br /> <br /> Not my cup of tea, but it seems right up your alley.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T09:48:39-07:00","id":1077035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1077023#post1077023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, Nyrufa, I'm pretty sure you would enjoy Mage the Asenscion more than Mage the Awakening. As I understand it, Mage the Asenscion's Magic works based on consensual reality. The more people believe a thing, and the harder they believe it, the more it becomes true. There are certain trends in magical practices (called paradigms) not because those practices are magically potent <i>per se</i>, but because getting a lot of mages believing in the same magical paradigm <i>makes it</i> magically potent. Muggle witnesses can fuck up magical effects that are obviously impossible in their worldview because their collective disbelief in it can cause it to not be possible. And the technocracy that you felt would turn you off of the game is an antagonist group. Mages who use a technology-based magical paradigm and promote advancement of and access to technology among non-magic folk so as to strengthen their own paradigm and weaken others.<br /> <br /> Not my cup of tea, but it seems right up your alley.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sounds good, especially since the old games were stand alone, meaning I don't have to search for a bunch of other books. Does it have a 20th anniversary book, yet?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T10:16:20-07:00","id":1077048,"title":"","content":"It does have a 20th anniversary book. I heard it's pretty good, but I dislike oWoD mechanics, so I never picked it up. It's also pretty expensive.<br /> <br /> As for magic - <br /> See, for me, magic was always about intellectual discovery and using your knowledge to do things. Navigating occult rules, discovering configurations that produce certain results, and so on; you discover a magical system, and then devote your intellect to obtain system mastery of it so great, that you can create specific results. It resonates with me a lot.<br /> <br /> I can hardly see &quot;Will Working&quot; as a &quot;my magic&quot;, because it feels like a celebration of stubborness and denial. I never liked that super-quoted phrase of rejecting your reality and replacing it with your own. It feels...I don't know, only way I can say it without sounding offensive is the thing I said above - celebration and glorification of denial. I can see why it can be seen as magic, but if you asked me to describe magic, I would never even *think* about it in the first place. I would probably place it as a specific supernatural power like vampirism or something.<br /> <br /> So I really like Demon and God Machine from the fluff perspective...<br /> ...but I dislike Demon as a game, because I just can't bear it's mechanics. Which is a goddamn shame, because thematically, I find it interesting, almost interesting enough to play inherently inhuman character of Demon instead of post-humans like Vampires or Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T10:40:40-07:00","id":1077063,"title":"","content":"As a small counter-point, the Will Working in Mage the Awakening IS 'believing' in something so hard that it becomes real; it's just that that's how it works PER casting. You want to form a fireball, you imagine a fireball so hard that it pops into existence. The difference is that aside for each casting of a spell, reality isn't consensual so the world is what it is most of the time. That means that a Mage can imagine that Fireball once and see how it interacts with the world and then change how they imagine the fireball a little differently next time based on that observation and improve their ability to cast. <br /> <br /> Now the world in this case includes Symbols of reality that are the method that Mages use to cast in the first place, so the refining of their spells is done by greater understanding of the Symbols involved (because everything is based on the Symbols so all increases in understanding are in way greater understanding of the Symbols).<br /> <br /> And while I'm not an expert on Mage: the Ascension, although it does have consensual reality, it still takes more for a Mage to increase the power of their spells than just 'believing harder'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T10:46:23-07:00","id":1077067,"title":"","content":"A counter point to counter point. It's manipulating symbolism by crafting carefully prepared Imago that incorporates symbols capable of rewriting reality and rotating them into a configuration that will produce the desired effect. Even if the knowledge you need to produce the result and the process in which you do so can be intuitive on soul-deep level, it's still a magical procedure that doesn't rely on your &quot;belief&quot;. It's an informed act of, well, wizardry.<br /> Then again, I believe I don't posses the ability to &quot;imagine&quot; in the way most people do, so maybe it's why I can't draw a connection between &quot;believe&quot; and &quot;form a spell&quot; the way Awakening does it.<br /> <br /> Like, I don't need to &quot;believe&quot; in order to write this post, but understanding how to manipulate the forum software (I HATE IT WITH PASSION HOTTER THAN CORE OF A RAGING STAR) and knowledge of English definitely are necessary to make it reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":9102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","user":"WHW","date":". 04-12-2017, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T14:18:59-07:00","id":1077209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1077067#post1077067\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A counter point to counter point. It's manipulating symbolism by crafting carefully prepared Imago that incorporates symbols capable of rewriting reality and rotating them into a configuration that will produce the desired effect. Even if the knowledge you need to produce the result and the process in which you do so can be intuitive on soul-deep level, it's still a magical procedure that doesn't rely on your &quot;belief&quot;. It's an informed act of, well, wizardry.<br /> Then again, I believe I don't posses the ability to &quot;imagine&quot; in the way most people do, so maybe it's why I can't draw a connection between &quot;believe&quot; and &quot;form a spell&quot; the way Awakening does it.<br /> <br /> Like, I don't need to &quot;believe&quot; in order to write this post, but understanding how to manipulate the forum software (I HATE IT WITH PASSION HOTTER THAN CORE OF A RAGING STAR) and knowledge of English definitely are necessary to make it reality.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The difference there I would say, is that in Awakening you need to be able to envision the post in its entirety in your mind, every letter, every space, every punctuation BEFORE it can become reality. You can't see it with your physical eyes part way through and adjust, you have to do it all in your head. The knowledge of Symbols helps as does the various Yantras that you can do to trigger it in your mind better. But ultimatley the spell 'exists' in your head before it does in reality.<br /> <br /> oh, and I put 'believe' in quotes in the previous post because it is not really the word I would choose to use, but was appropriate for the conversation. I actually have no concept of belief as I understand it to mean. 'Envision with perfect acuity and then enforce that vision on reality' is a more accurate (though wordy) way of putting it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":1329,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","user":"ElvesofZion","date":". 04-12-2017, 05:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:37:03-07:00","id":1077285,"title":"","content":"Come to think of it, couldn't the mages in Ascension build a time machine to go back and stop the Age of Order from happening?<br /> <br /> Sure, conventional wisdom says that time travel is impossible, but that's the point of view from the Technocracy. Other mages believe in a mutable reality, and there are a hell of a lot of people who believe / want to believe in the possibility of time travel. I don't think it would be too difficult to whip together a machine that could do the trick.<br /> <br /> <br /> And, much like when humans experimented by launching animals into space, the mages could do the same thing by transporting animals through different points in time until they managed to work out the kinks and stop the machine from exploding or whatever happens during Paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:42:44-07:00","id":1077291,"title":"","content":"The Technocracy would probably stop them. They have Terminators for that kind of thing. They're mages too, they just stick to their paradigm of 'science' so they're more likely to get time machines anyhow.<br /> <br /> You could probably get more information in the Ascension board.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:45:57-07:00","id":1077294,"title":"","content":"Sure, the Technocracy could have stuff in place to stop them. But if you travel back far enough to before the Age of Order took place, then it stands to reason mutable reality would still be at its peak. So any mage who survived the trip would be far more powerful than they would be in present day. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T15:57:13-07:00","id":1077303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1077294#post1077294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, the Technocracy could have stuff in place to stop them. But if you travel back far enough to before the Age of Order took place, then it stands to reason mutable reality would still be at its peak. So any mage who survived the trip would be far more powerful than they would be in present day. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>But so would any Technocrats who followed. And chances are, they've probably already thought of it. In general, the rule for the Old World of Darkness is that the players are gonna lose in the long run.<br /> <br /> Unless the 20th Anniversary editions changed that at all. I haven't seen those, and I'm just going off the old books my mom still has.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://eoinsstuff.shoutwiki.com/wiki/Genius:_the_Transgression_(2nd_Edition)\" target=\"_blank\">Genius: the Transgression 2E is a thing that's being worked on.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4488-malonkey1","name":"malonkey1","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4488_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T16:08:48-07:00","id":1077316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>malonkey1</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1077303#post1077303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But so would any Technocrats who followed. And chances are, they've probably already thought of it. In general, the rule for the Old World of Darkness is that the players are gonna lose in the long run.<br /> <br /> Unless the 20th Anniversary editions changed that at all. I haven't seen those, and I'm just going off the old books my mom still has.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure, they'd probably be more powerful. But most of the world doesn't know about / acknowledge their view of reality being scientific and quantifiable. Time travel would, in effect, reverse the roles of any mages who attempted it. The Technocracy would suddenly find themselves in a period where the rest of the world still believes in magic and superstition, making their technological applications more difficult. Before the AoO, mages were running wild with their magic, so any mage attempting to flee / thwart the Technocracy would suddenly have far greater leeway in their casting with the threat of Paradox is decreased.<br /> <br /> <br /> I guess the reason why the game doesn't explore the possibility is because the WoD largely revolves around players getting the short end of the stick, and that's hard to convey if they can go back to a point and undo their enemies before they rise to power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T18:20:27-07:00","id":1077382,"title":"","content":"They would be about equal in the past. Technocracy thing isn't that they are stronger because non Mages believe in science, it's that they managed to create a united paradigm for everyone in the world which replaced a sea of reality bubbles that varied from a village to village. <br /> One of reasons why I dislike oWoD is it's habit of antagonizing &quot;adult&quot; and &quot;not-like-old&quot; things - technology in both Mage and Werewolf, psychology and psychiatry (!) in Changeling, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T18:32:23-07:00","id":1077389,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1077382#post1077382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They would be about equal in the past. Technocracy thing isn't that they are stronger because non Mages believe in science, it's that they managed to create a united paradigm for everyone in the world which replaced a sea of reality bubbles that varied from a village to village.<br /> One of reasons why I dislike oWoD is it's habit of antagonizing &quot;adult&quot; and &quot;not-like-old&quot; things - technology in both Mage and Werewolf, psychology and psychiatry (!) in Changeling, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I've seen a lot of reviewers complain about Dreaming in the past because it doesn't seem World of <b>Darkness</b> material. But I have to disagree completely, I actually think it fits perfectly if you look at it from a <b>coming of age</b> story perspective. In your youth, the world seems bright, colorful and anything is possible. But as time passes by, you're exposed to cynicism and the cruelty of the outside world. Which gradually transforms you into something just as cynical as the people around you.<br /> <br /> Dreaming is horribly depressing and out of all the splat settings, it is the one I would never want to live in. But at the same time, that feeling of loss and sadness that it provokes from me is the reason why I think it fits perfectly with the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:13:34-07:00","id":1077419,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1077389#post1077389\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I've seen a lot of reviewers complain about Dreaming in the past because it doesn't seem World of <b>Darkness</b> material. But I have to disagree completely, I actually think it fits perfectly if you look at it from a <b>coming of age</b> story perspective. In your youth, the world seems bright, colorful and anything is possible. But as time passes by, you're exposed to cynicism and the cruelty of the outside world. Which gradually transforms you into something just as cynical as the people around you.<br /> <br /> Dreaming is horribly depressing and out of all the splat settings, it is the one I would never want to live in. But at the same time, that feeling of loss and sadness that it provokes from me is the reason why I think it fits perfectly with the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Have you read Wraith: the Oblivion, yet? Because that's considered the grimmest of the (o)WoD to most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:19:04-07:00","id":1077424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1077419#post1077419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Have you read Wraith: the Oblivion, yet? Because that's considered the grimmest of the (o)WoD to most.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nah, being absorbed into the void of nothingness and ceasing to exist seems pretty peaceful to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-12T19:29:21-07:00","id":1077432,"title":"","content":"Not gonna talk about Dreaming, because anything I have to say about it would make me sound uncomfortably antagonistic, as I have nothing good to say about it. And I already get bashed for writing about games that I *like* when I'm not 100% uncritical about them, so I don't want to think what would happen if I started talking about something I actively find bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T06:54:44-07:00","id":1077700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1077209#post1077209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The difference there I would say, is that in Awakening you need to be able to envision the post in its entirety in your mind, every letter, every space, every punctuation BEFORE it can become reality. You can't see it with your physical eyes part way through and adjust, you have to do it all in your head. The knowledge of Symbols helps as does the various Yantras that you can do to trigger it in your mind better. But ultimatley the spell 'exists' in your head before it does in reality.<br /> <br /> oh, and I put 'believe' in quotes in the previous post because it is not really the word I would choose to use, but was appropriate for the conversation. I actually have no concept of belief as I understand it to mean. 'Envision with perfect acuity and then enforce that vision on reality' is a more accurate (though wordy) way of putting it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incorrect. Awakened magic manifests from the intimate knowledge that there is a higher realm above this fallen reality without the shade of a cosmic cancer preventing you from calling and shaping that fire in the form of an explosive ball, using symbology to cement that higher expression in the here and now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T07:43:48-07:00","id":1077729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1077700#post1077700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Incorrect. Awakened magic manifests from the intimate knowledge that there is a higher realm above this fallen reality without the shade of a cosmic cancer preventing you from calling and shaping that fire in the form of an explosive ball, using symbology to cement that higher expression in the here and now.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure what you said here that contradicts anything I said. You are referencing detail;s of the cosmology that I left vague (on purpose since Nyrufa is not familiar with Awakening) but I spoke about the process a mage goes through in the moment of casting a spell, which is based on the cosmology that you are referencing but that wasn't the point. I was describing the process of forming an Imago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T07:49:23-07:00","id":1077733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1077209#post1077209\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The difference there I would say, is that in Awakening you need to be able to envision the post in its entirety in your mind, every letter, every space, every punctuation BEFORE it can become reality. You can't see it with your physical eyes part way through and adjust, you have to do it all in your head. The knowledge of Symbols helps as does the various Yantras that you can do to trigger it in your mind better. But ultimatley the spell 'exists' in your head before it does in reality.<br /> <br /> oh, and I put 'believe' in quotes in the previous post because it is not really the word I would choose to use, but was appropriate for the conversation. I actually have no concept of belief as I understand it to mean. 'Envision with perfect acuity and then enforce that vision on reality' is a more accurate (though wordy) way of putting it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I can't really comment on that because the process you describe here is very visual and thus alien to me, but so is the general idea of having an Imago in mind. That's why I constantly fall back on the planning/coding/writing analogies instead of &quot;picture in your mind&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T08:03:43-07:00","id":1077744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1077733#post1077733\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, I can't really comment on that because the process you describe here is very visual and thus alien to me, but so is the general idea of having an Imago in mind. That's why I constantly fall back on the planning/coding/writing analogies instead of &quot;picture in your mind&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I know you have commented on that before. I don't mean to harp on it or anything. Just trying to be sure Nyrufa gets my point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-13T21:56:39-07:00","id":1078176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1076453#post1076453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Real world science refuses to acknowledge my ideas of magic and the supernatural. So I naturally learned to view magic and science as two different things.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have the opposite experience - I come from a cultural background where repairing a car engine with the proper tools and a mystic dance to help a wound heal faster are both considered magical rituals, where throwing a temper tantrum is an offering to spirits, where adding kindling to a fire was to make it more enticing for the flame to enter it. My early life, as far as I can tell, was steeped in magic - My uncle once sent me out to catch and kill him a rattlesnake, and when I brought it back he told me how us dragonslayers were a dying breed. He once sent me on a quest into town to get him a six-pack of beer and some smokes; it took two days and I was rewarded with stories about the conversations Panther and Wind had before the world was created. I was taught that every action you partook was a ritual and the result was the return of that ritual. I had to learn the typical &quot;magic vs. technology&quot; meme post-hoc, and it when I was first trying to learn it, <i>it seemed insane</i>. Like, if X clearly happened when you did Y, was that not the successful outcome of the ritual, whether you were flipping a lightswitch or chopping at a tree with an axe?<br /> <br /> Clarke's Third Law gets snowcloned a lot, and he better explains it in his works - it means that anything, given the proper context, is technology. How does your iPhone work? It may as well be attended by invisible blue pixies that cast dust upon it to make the screen light up for all you know or care.<br /> <br /> (as a side note, I used to hear stories of demon owls named &quot;Steekeenee&quot; that change bodies by vomiting their shadows into their victims and have a magic power that lets them concentrate all your blood into your heart before they tear it out and eat it; they were terrifying as a child and I was convinced there was one that followed me around - I was notably disturbed when Strix Chronicle came out)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4170-raygungoth","name":"raygungoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4170_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T01:06:12-07:00","id":1078216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1077285#post1077285\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Come to think of it, couldn't the mages in Ascension build a time machine to go back and stop the Age of Order from happening?<br /> Sure, conventional wisdom says that time travel is impossible, but that's the point of view from the Technocracy. Other mages believe in a mutable reality, and there are a hell of a lot of people who believe / want to believe in the possibility of time travel. I don't think it would be too difficult to whip together a machine that could do the trick.<br /> And, much like when humans experimented by launching animals into space, the mages could do the same thing by transporting animals through different points in time until they managed to work out the kinks and stop the machine from exploding or whatever happens during Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>Paradox isn't controllable and it tends to crush any magi who play with time travel. Further, if you succeed, you essentially spin off a seperate version of reality into the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Also, from a narrative point of view, going back to time to stop the OoR is missing the point. There's no single conspiracy that leads to the modern world, the OoR is a movement and eventually a system; you can murder all the grandmasters of the order and the thing will keep going.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T04:10:01-07:00","id":1078265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1078216#post1078216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Paradox isn't controllable and it tends to crush any magi who play with time travel. Further, if you succeed, you essentially spin off a seperate version of reality into the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Also, from a narrative point of view, going back to time to stop the OoR is missing the point. There's no single conspiracy that leads to the modern world, the OoR is a movement and eventually a system; you can murder all the grandmasters of the order and the thing will keep going.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, yeah, there's two popular versions of time travel. In one version, you literally travel through time and any changes you make will impact the future you return to. In the other version, you just travel to an alternate reality where things played out differently than they should have. So any changes you make in the new time line won't affect the existing time line you came from. Either one sounds good, actually.And the alternate reality method would probably be less risky than the rewriting history method.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T06:57:12-07:00","id":1078313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1078265#post1078265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, yeah, there's two popular versions of time travel. In one version, you literally travel through time and any changes you make will impact the future you return to. In the other version, you just travel to an alternate reality where things played out differently than they should have. So any changes you make in the new time line won't affect the existing time line you came from. Either one sounds good, actually.And the alternate reality method would probably be less risky than the rewriting history method.</div> </div> </div> </div>Logically, the Alternate Reality one is the only one of the two that will work. If you &quot;changed history&quot;, then &quot;you&quot; don't exist anymore. If you Bob-the-Mage went back in time in 2013 to stop WWII, then why would Bob-the-Mage in the new WWII-less timeline travel back in time to stop something that didn't happen? Temporal Paradox.<br /> <br /> Best bet is to change something, then &quot;return&quot; to the future by sticking yourself in stasis. Of course, then it still isn't &quot;your&quot; future/present anymore, so I don't know why you'd bother.<br /> <br /> Time travel - only a good idea while drunk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T07:20:06-07:00","id":1078332,"title":"","content":"The real reason the whole &quot;travel back before the Age of Order and prevent the Technocracy from happening&quot; doesn't work is because Wrinkle the Paradox Spirit will imprison you outside of Time until you say sorry for trying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/274-enokh","name":"Enokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T08:18:28-07:00","id":1078364,"title":"","content":"The Asenscion talk is getting pretty off topic...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T08:53:42-07:00","id":1078384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1078265#post1078265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Well, yeah, there's two popular versions of time travel. In one version, you literally travel through time and any changes you make will impact the future you return to. In the other version, you just travel to an alternate reality where things played out differently than they should have. So any changes you make in the new time line won't affect the existing time line you came from. Either one sounds good, actually.And the alternate reality method would probably be less risky than the rewriting history method.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which <b><i>Feng Shui</i></b> solves with the idea of Critical Shifts... Is an interesting application of time travel theory. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T09:05:00-07:00","id":1078386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1078364#post1078364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Asenscion talk is getting pretty off topic...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> At this point, what <b>is</b> on topic?<br /> <br /> We could go back to discussing the God-Machine and its implications on science, technology and the supernatural.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T09:54:33-07:00","id":1078407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1078364#post1078364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Asenscion talk is getting pretty off topic...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not necessarily. The whole topic was written because I disagreed with GMC's idea of magic, so alternative approaches to it in other game lines seems fitting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1078313#post1078313\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Logically, the Alternate Reality one is the only one of the two that will work. If you &quot;changed history&quot;, then &quot;you&quot; don't exist anymore. If you Bob-the-Mage went back in time in 2013 to stop WWII, then why would Bob-the-Mage in the new WWII-less timeline travel back in time to stop something that didn't happen? Temporal Paradox.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Best bet is to change something, then &quot;return&quot; to the future by sticking yourself in stasis. Of course, then it still isn't &quot;your&quot; future/present anymore, so I don't know why you'd bother.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Time travel - only a good idea while drunk.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;Big ball of wibbly, wobbly, timey whimey... stuff.&quot; - Doctor Who<br /> <br /> One could go with the esoteric idea that time is an artificial concept, created by the Technocracy to prevent anybody from tampering with their work.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T09:59:37-07:00","id":1078408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1078407#post1078407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One could go with the esoteric idea that time is an artificial concept, created by the Technocracy to prevent anybody from tampering with their work.[/SIZE][/FONT]</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> To bring somewhat back to Chronicles, Time Travel in Mage: The Awakening follows this to a degree (in 2nd Ed at least). Linear Time is part of the Lie, which is why Mages can manipulate it. Mages are explicitly immune to their own temporal paradoxes and there is a spell that would shield you from all time travel caused revisions to history.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T12:02:24-07:00","id":1078453,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ElvesofZion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1078408#post1078408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To bring somewhat back to Chronicles, Time Travel in Mage: The Awakening follows this to a degree (in 2nd Ed at least). Linear Time is part of the Lie, which is why Mages can manipulate it. Mages are explicitly immune to their own temporal paradoxes and there is a spell that would shield you from all time travel caused revisions to history.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't really agree that linear time is part of the lie, honestly. In the same way that Death isn't part of the lie, Time is an Arcanum, so it is part of the Supernal truth. What's a lie is that what is past is passed and cannot be undone. But even when manipulating time through the Time Arcanum, it behaves linearly. The lie is that time is like a river, ever flowing only one way, the truth is that time is like a tapestry in the weaving, the past being that which has already been woven, the future being that which has yet to be woven, and the present being the point where the weaving occurs. But like a tapestry, if you mess up a stitch you can unwravel it to that point and do it again differently.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T12:30:13-07:00","id":1078472,"title":"","content":"Half serious:<br /> Future literally not existing also means that your players don't have to be paranoid about future mages post-emptively dropping a nuke on them, as there are no future mages to do so!<br /> ...which, on the other hand, means that if something from future *does* impact you, it means that whatever you are feeling right now is not right now and is just timeline sorting itself out. Weird realization. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T13:04:37-07:00","id":1078492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1078453#post1078453\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I wouldn't really agree that linear time is part of the lie, honestly. In the same way that Death isn't part of the lie, Time is an Arcanum, so it is part of the Supernal truth. What's a lie is that what is past is passed and cannot be undone. But even when manipulating time through the Time Arcanum, it behaves linearly. The lie is that time is like a river, ever flowing only one way, the truth is that time is like a tapestry in the weaving, the past being that which has already been woven, the future being that which has yet to be woven, and the present being the point where the weaving occurs. But like a tapestry, if you mess up a stitch you can unwravel it to that point and do it again differently.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, yeah, that is a lot better of a way to put it. But I am at work and went for brevity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>(he/him/his)<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Backer #2010","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1329-elvesofzion","name":"ElvesofZion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1329_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T16:01:36-07:00","id":1078608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WHW</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1078472#post1078472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Half serious:<br /> Future literally not existing also means that your players don't have to be paranoid about future mages post-emptively dropping a nuke on them, as there are no future mages to do so!<br /> ...which, on the other hand, means that if something from future *does* impact you, it means that whatever you are feeling right now is not right now and is just timeline sorting itself out. Weird realization. </div> </div> </div> </div>Yup. It would be pretty existentially horrifying as a Mage to meet a Mage from the future, because you would know with absolute certainty that you are literally living in the objective past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-14T18:08:56-07:00","id":1078679,"title":"","content":"You could even make a case for it not being &quot;living&quot;, but simply being a rewritten memory of someone in the future. Right in this &quot;second&quot;, the world is simply readjusting it's timeline to consequences created by a time traveler! Trip trip trippity trip.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/9102-whw","name":"WHW","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar9102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2542"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-15T00:02:10-07:00","id":1078786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1075671-another-gmc-tangent?p=1078608#post1078608\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup. It would be pretty existentially horrifying as a Mage to meet a Mage from the future, because you would know with absolute certainty that you are literally living in the objective past.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so sure. I mean, it's certainly annoying having time travellers turn up, but aside from that you're not going to notice any differences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}